Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching a Qubit: The Quantum-Bayesian Approach to Continuous Measurement, \
from One Qubit to Entanglement\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["A weak continuous measurement never collapses a qubit \
outright. It trickles information out through a noisy detector current, and \
the observer folds each noisy reading back into the state with Bayes' rule. \
This essay builds the quantum-Bayesian update from primitives, runs it, and \
then generalizes it twice. Part I is one qubit under one detector: a frozen \
qubit localizing by accumulating likelihood, a pure state staying exactly \
pure along a single record while the ensemble dephases, a Rabi drive \
interleaved as a symmetric split, a non-ideal detector capping the purity, \
the output spectrum whose coherent line can never rise more than four times \
above the noise floor, and the phase back-action a general detector adds, \
ending on the Kraus operator both generalizations grow from. Part II points a \
second detector at a different axis, so the two Bayes kicks stop commuting \
and the state stops collapsing and starts diffusing on the Bloch sphere. Part \
III gives one detector two qubits and a blind spot, so a measurement alone \
drives them into a Bell state. Each generalization is carried out against a \
real superconducting-qubit experiment: the single-qubit trajectories of Murch \
and Siddiqi, the simultaneous non-commuting measurement of Hacohen-Gourgy and \
co-workers, and the remote measurement-induced entanglement of Roch and \
co-workers.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 18, 2026)", "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["\<\
Notation and Conventions: The Detector, the Record, and the Rates\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We work in units where the reduced Planck constant is one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 ". The qubit is written in the measured (localized) basis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " that the detector couples to, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "1", ",", "0", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "0", ",", "1", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 ", so the density matrix is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " and the single monitored coordinate is the population difference ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ". A qubit density matrix carries three real numbers, the Bloch vector; the \
detector reads out only the projection ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 ", and the other two ride along in the coherence."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The detector emits a current whose short-time average over a window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 ". Its two calibrated outputs are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 " for a qubit definitely in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " for one definitely in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 ". For a general state, a linear detector therefore has the \
population-weighted mean"
}], "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 ", the populations are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 ". Substitution separates the mean into a state-independent midpoint and a \
qubit-dependent signal,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]}], "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "-", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]}], "2"], " ", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The actual record fluctuates around this mean. Defining the midpoint ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " and detector response ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 ", and writing the zero-mean white noise as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ", gives"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "2"], " ", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]}], "2"], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 " is zero-mean white detector noise. In the single-sided convention used \
here,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
     StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ideal white noise has no finite pointwise variance; only a record averaged \
over a nonzero time window is an ordinary random variable. Over the same \
window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " used to define ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", define"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], 
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell["The averaged noise is Gaussian, with", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["Var",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "_"], 
        StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Thus a longer averaging window suppresses the detector noise: the variance \
decreases as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " and the standard deviation as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 ". The limits make the construction explicit: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " returns the mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 ", while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell["What Is Set, What Is Measured, and What Is Derived", "Subsection",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell["\<\
At a fixed detector operating point, the quantities have different roles:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Calibrated detector quantities:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 ", the noise spectral density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 ", and the total ensemble dephasing rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " are obtained from separate experimental calibrations."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Chosen controls:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the averaging window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " is selected by the observer or numerical protocol, while the Rabi \
frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " is set by the qubit drive."
}], "Item",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Derived quantities:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ", the averaged-noise variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ", the measurement rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 ", the measurement time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 ", the extra dephasing rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 ", and the efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 " follow from the calibrated quantities."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Random and dynamical quantities:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " is a random outcome, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " are the conditioned qubit state inferred from the accumulated record."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The word ",
 StyleBox["calibrated", "TI"],
 " is more precise here than ",
 StyleBox["fundamental", "TI"],
 ". Experimental controls such as detector bias, measurement power, and \
amplifier gain establish an operating point. The effective model then takes \
the measured values ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " at that operating point as inputs."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Step 1: Calibrate the signal contrast.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Prepare the qubit in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " separately and measure the corresponding mean outputs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 ". Their midpoint and separation are then fixed:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]}], "2"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Once ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " have been calibrated, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " are not additional independent parameters."
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Step 2: Calibrate the noise, then choose a window.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Measure the flat part of the detector's single-sided noise spectrum to \
obtain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ". The observer then chooses a finite averaging window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 ". This choice produces the ordinary Gaussian variance"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
    StyleBox["Var",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "_"], 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The detector property is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 "; the analysis choice is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 "; and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " is derived from both. Making ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 " smaller makes each individual reading noisier, but it also produces more \
readings per unit time. It does not change the detector's intrinsic \
information-acquisition rate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the white-noise model, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " must be longer than the detector correlation time. For a discrete \
weak-measurement step with a driven qubit, it should also be short enough \
that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[LessLess]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[LessLess]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Step 3: Derive the measurement rate.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Over a window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 ", the two possible readout distributions are Gaussians with the same \
variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " and with means separated by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", 
       StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]], 
    StyleBox["exp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", "}"}], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell["Their overlap is", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\|01d4aa", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}], "\[Infinity]"], 
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "=", 
    StyleBox["exp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{"8", 
       StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]}], "]", "=", 
    StyleBox["exp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{"4", 
       StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], "]"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the measurement rate by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d4aa", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 ". It follows that"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This formula says that information arrives faster when the two detector \
outputs are farther apart and slower when the detector is noisier. The units \
also work: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " has units of current squared times time, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 " has units of inverse time. Only two of the three quantities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 " are independent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell["The conventional measurement time is", "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The factor of two is a convention worth keeping visible. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ", the two Gaussian means are separated by twice their common standard \
deviation. The likelihood overlap decays on the related time scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Step 4: Calibrate total ensemble dephasing.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Repeat the experiment many times and ignore the individual detector \
records. The ensemble-averaged coherence decays as"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"], 
          StyleBox["(",
           SpanMaxSize->1], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[")",
           SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
         StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
        StyleBox["records",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[Proportional]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Thus ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " is measured independently of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 ". Quantum mechanics requires the total dephasing associated with this \
measurement model to satisfy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ": the qubit cannot reveal information in the accessible record without \
losing at least the corresponding ensemble coherence. The difference and \
ratio define"
}], "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "-", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}], ",", 
     "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "\[Element]", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}]}]}]}]}], "]"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " is the rate of information that reaches the observer, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " is dephasing whose information is not present in the observed record, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " is the fraction of the total dephasing that is accounted for by acquired \
information. Equivalently,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "-", "1"}], ")"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a quantum-limited detector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ". A non-ideal detector has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 " and therefore destroys ensemble coherence faster than its observed record \
acquires information."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Step 5: Keep detector symmetry separate from qubit symmetry.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " For the symmetric detector used first in this essay, the output noise and \
phase back-action are uncorrelated. There is therefore no record-correlated \
unitary phase kick. In the ideal case, the conditioned back-action is purely \
informational and moves the state along Bloch-sphere meridians; if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 ", the unobserved part still contributes the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 ". This detector assumption is distinct from the symmetric-qubit assumption \
of zero energy bias. With that qubit choice, the controlled Hamiltonian is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"q", "b"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
      StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " is an externally set Rabi frequency, not a quantity derived from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell["The physical calibration chain is therefore", "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "}", "\[LongRightArrow]", "{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "}"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "}", "\[LongRightArrow]", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], ",", 
     "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]], ",", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "}", "\[LongRightArrow]", "{", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "}"}], "."}]}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell["The Detector Noise as a Wolfram Process", "Subsection",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Notation stated the noise's features: zero mean, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Prime]"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " correlation, the single-sided density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ", and the window-averaged variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 ". In a computation-first account these are not taken on faith; we build the \
noise from Wolfram's own process objects and read each feature back off them. \
Two built-ins carry everything. The pointwise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 " has no ordinary variance, but its running integral does, and that integral \
is a Wiener process (Brownian motion, \"integrated white Gaussian noise\" in \
its own documentation): one derivative in each time turns its covariance back \
into the correlation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 ". The window average, by contrast, is already an ordinary random variable, \
one independent Gaussian draw per window, which is exactly a discrete-time \
white-noise process. Everything below is read off these two objects. In code \
the single-sided density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 " is written ",
 Cell[BoxData["ss"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 " and the window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["tau"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 ", and the two sample times are ",
 Cell[BoxData["t1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["t2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the running integral. The noise accumulated over time is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"WienerProcess", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"S", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 ", its volatility ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " fixed so the variance builds at the two-sided noise level; read its mean \
and its covariance:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"WienerProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"ss", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"w", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"CovarianceFunction", "[", 
        RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", "t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The integrated noise is unbiased, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ", and its covariance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["min",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 ", the signature of Brownian motion: two times share only the history up to \
the earlier one. Because this process is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 ", differentiating that shared-history covariance once in each time must \
return the pointwise correlation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " itself."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Do that differentiation. Written as a smooth part plus a kink, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["min",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], "-", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 ", the smooth part differentiates away and the kink carries the spike, since \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[DoublePrime]"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"CovarianceFunction", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"WienerProcess", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"ss", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "t1", ",", 
         " ", "t2"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
         RowBox[{"p_", ",", " ", "q_"}], "]"}], " ", ":>", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"p", " ", "+", " ", "q", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p", " ", "-", " ", "q"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}],
       ",", " ", "t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Derivative", "[", "2", "]"}], "[", "Abs", "]"}], "[", "r_", 
      "]"}], " ", ":>", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DiracDelta", "[", "r", "]"}]}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There it is: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 ", the single-sided correlation the Notation posited, now read off the \
integral of the noise rather than assumed. Note that the naive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"D", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
     RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 " returns zero, dropping the distributional spike: the delta lives entirely \
in the kink of the covariance, which is why we split that kink out before \
differentiating."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell["\<\
A delta correlation is white by definition, so its power spectrum, the \
Fourier transform of the correlation in the lag, is flat. Fourier-transform \
the correlation just derived, with the second time fixed at zero so it \
becomes a function of the lag alone:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2", ",", " ", "w"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FourierTransform", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"D", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"CovarianceFunction", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"WienerProcess", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"ss", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "t1", ",", 
           " ", "t2"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
           RowBox[{"p_", ",", " ", "q_"}], "]"}], " ", ":>", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"p", " ", "+", " ", "q", " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
              RowBox[{"p", " ", "-", " ", "q"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
           "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"t2", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", "t1", ",", " ", 
     "w", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The spectrum is flat at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 ", equal power at every frequency, which is what \"white\" means; that flat \
two-sided level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 " folds onto positive frequencies as the single-sided density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 ", the convention this essay keeps throughout."
}], "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the window average, the object that does have a finite variance. It is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 ", so its variance is the Brownian variance at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 " divided by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 ", put in by nothing but the integral:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"WienerProcess", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ss", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "tau", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
  RowBox[{"tau", "^", "2"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The variance is the derived ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 ": a longer window suppresses the noise as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 ", not by assumption but because the Brownian variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 " is spread over the whole window."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That averaged noise is itself a discrete-time white-noise process, one \
independent normal draw of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " per window; read its three defining features off the object at once:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"noise", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"WhiteNoiseProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"noise", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
        RowBox[{"noise", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"CovarianceFunction", "[", 
        RowBox[{"noise", ",", " ", "t1", ",", " ", "t2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Zero mean, variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],
 ", and a covariance of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 " at zero lag and nothing off it: ",
 Cell[BoxData["CovarianceFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " hands back a ",
 Cell[BoxData["DiscreteDelta"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ", the discrete image of the continuous Dirac correlation, so successive \
windows are genuinely independent draws."
}], "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell["\<\
The reading is that averaged noise riding on the deterministic signal, one \
transformed process whose mean carries the state and whose spread is the \
noise the state must beat. Read its mean and variance; its correlation is the \
discrete delta of the white-noise process it is built from, which a \
transformed process does not re-expose, so only these two are read here:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"xi", ",", " ", "t1"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"current", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"TransformedProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ic", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"dI", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "z"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"xi", "[", "t1", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"xi", " ", "\[Distributed]", " ", 
          RowBox[{"WhiteNoiseProcess", "[", 
           RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",",
          " ", "t1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"current", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
        RowBox[{"current", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 " and the variance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 ": the deterministic part carries every bit of the state dependence and the \
process carries all of the randomness, and the two never mix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same reading in continuous time, before any window average, is a \
stochastic differential equation: the accumulated signal obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "2"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 ", an Ito process whose drift is the deterministic level and whose single \
Wiener increment carries the noise. Read how its mean and variance grow in \
time:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"xx", ",", " ", "t1"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"proc", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"ic", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"dI", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "z"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"ss", "/", "2"}], "]"}], "}"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"xx", "[", "t1", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", "xx", "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"proc", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Variance", "[", 
        RowBox[{"proc", "[", "t1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The accumulated signal's mean grows as the deterministic level times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " and its variance as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ", the Brownian variance once more; divide that variance by the window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " and the per-window spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " comes back, so the continuous equation and the discrete window average are \
one and the same noise seen at two time scales."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, the two extremes of the mean recover the detector's own calibrated \
levels; evaluate the signal at the poles ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", "i1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dI", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"i0", " ", "-", " ", "i1"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ic", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"i0", " ", "+", " ", "i1"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"ic", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"dI", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "#"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], 
       " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],
 ", so the mean interpolates linearly between the two calibrated levels while \
the window sets how sharply the noise lets them be told apart. The next \
section fixes these levels numerically to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], "=", "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 " and turns this noise into a runnable measurement step."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],

Cell["The Numerical Toolkit: From Calibration to a Runnable Step", \
"Subsection",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the numerical examples, it is convenient to reverse one part of this \
chain and use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " as the time unit. We normalize the detector outputs to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], "=", "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 ", and then infer the equivalent noise density from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"dI", ",", " ", "i0", ",", " ", "i1", ",", " ", "ic"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"i0", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"i1", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"i0", " ", "-", " ", "i1"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ic", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"i0", " ", "+", " ", "i1"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", "i1", ",", " ", "dI"}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the two conditioned means sit symmetrically about zero, so \
a reading's sign is the only hint of which state produced it, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " is the full separation the noise must beat."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The chance that a state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],
 " produced a given reading is a Gaussian likelihood; define it as a function \
of the window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "gaussLike", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mu_", ",", " ", "var_", ",", " ", "ibar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "-", " ", "mu"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "var"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", "var"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell["\<\
This is the single probabilistic object the whole formalism turns on: \
everything downstream is Bayes' rule applied to these two likelihoods.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 " and the honest detector draw, sampling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 " from the Gaussian mixture ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], " ", "\|01d4a9", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], ",", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], " ", "\|01d4a9", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 " that the current state predicts:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"avgVar", ",", " ", "drawCurrent"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gm_", ",", " ", "tau_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dI", "^", "2"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", "gm"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "var_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", "i1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "    ", 
   
   RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "var", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In words, the detector first picks which bell to ring with the current \
populations as weights, then buries the level under Gaussian noise of \
variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],
 ". For the fixed detector used in these examples, increasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],
 " sharpens an individual averaged readout but does not alter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell["\<\
Now the heart of the formalism. The exact update over a step, in its cleanest \
form, keeps the populations Bayesian and lets each coherence carry the \
geometric mean of the two likelihoods, with an optional pure-dephasing factor \
for a non-ideal detector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], " ", "\[LongRightArrow]", " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], " ", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"k", "k"}], "TI"]], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], " ", "\[Times]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], " ", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"off", "-", 
       RowBox[{"diagonal", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "only"}]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}],
     FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["gaussLike",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], ",", 
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], ",", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell["\<\
Encode that update as one element-wise operation on the matrix:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "bayesUpdate", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "ibar_", ",", " ", "var_", ",", " ", "gt_"}], 
   "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"p0", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"p1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i1", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
     "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"p0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p0", " ", "p1"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p0", " ", "p1"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "p1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "/",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "p0"}], " ", "+",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "p1"}]}], 
       ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagonal entries pick up ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " and renormalize, which is textbook Gaussian Bayes on the populations; the \
off-diagonal entries pick up ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 ", so the coherence is pinned to the populations rather than measured \
directly."
}], "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm that this update is trace-preserving for any reading, symbolically, \
so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 " stays a density matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r00", ",", " ", "r01"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r01", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r00"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "gt"}], 
        "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "r00", " ", "<", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gt", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],

Cell["\<\
As expected, the two updated populations always sum to one: the normalizing \
denominator is exactly the predictive probability of the reading, so \
probability is conserved by construction.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],

Cell["\<\
A single step of the full dynamics interleaves a Hamiltonian half-rotation, \
the Bayesian kick, and another half-rotation, a symmetric (Strang) split that \
is second-order accurate in the step; for a frozen qubit the half-rotation is \
just the identity. Define the step, together with the readouts we will plot:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "measureStep", ",", " ", "blochVec", ",", " ", "purity", ",", " ", 
    "zComp"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"uHalf_", ",", " ", "var_", ",", " ", "gt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"uHalf", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uHalf", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"uHalf", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
       RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
         RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "var"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", 
        "gt"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uHalf", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVec", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "j", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zComp", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell["\<\
That is the entire integrator: a Gaussian draw, an element-wise Bayes kick, \
and two matrix products for the drive. For the output spectrum in Section 6 \
we will also want the record itself, so define a run that emits the stream of \
readings while it measures a driven qubit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "recordCurrents", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"recordCurrents", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "gm_", ",", " ", "tau_", ",", " ", "gt_", ",", " ", "om_", ",", " ", 
    "nst_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"uH", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"om", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FoldPairList", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "k"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"With", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"uH", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uH", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
             "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"With", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"ib", " ", "=", " ", 
                RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
              "       ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"uH", " ", ".", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                  "r1", ",", " ", "ib", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "gt"}], 
                  "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uH", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
             "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nst", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell["\<\
We will return to this record in Section 6; for now it is enough that each \
measurement produces a number, and the state and the record share the very \
same noise.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell["\<\
1. The Detector's Two Bells: Why One Look Cannot Separate Them\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A weak measurement is weak because a single short look is ambiguous. For a \
state that is definitely ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],
 " or definitely ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " the averaged current is a Gaussian centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 " with spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],
 "; the two bells overlap heavily until the window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],
 " is long enough to pull them apart, and the crossover scale is the \
measurement time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the two likelihoods ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 " against the reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 " for windows short, comparable to, and long relative to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"taum", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"dI", "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "gm"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"dI", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
             RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
               RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ibar"}], 
             "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
             RowBox[{"i1", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
               RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ibar"}], 
             "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "4"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Filling", " ", "->", " ", "Axis"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<averaged current\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<likelihood\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<window \[Tau] = \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
             RowBox[{"tau", "/", "taum"}], "]"}], " ", "<>", 
            " ", "\"\< \[Tau]m\>\""}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "240"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tau", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"taum", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "6"}], 
            "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Notice that at a quarter of the measurement time the two bells sit almost \
on top of each other, so a single reading barely favors either state; only as \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 " grows past ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 " do the peaks separate and a reading starts to mean something. Information \
is nothing but this shrinking overlap."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell["\<\
2. Populations Follow Bayes: Localization Without a Hamiltonian\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Switch off the Hamiltonian and the record can only report which state we \
are in, never rotate us between them. Start from the equatorial superposition \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{"0"},
       "Ket"], "+", 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
    SqrtBox["2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 ", whose two measured-basis populations are equal, and feed each reading \
through the update: the populations move by the likelihood ratio and drift \
toward one pole, a noisy random walk in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " rather than a jump. The pole that wins is random, with probability equal \
to the initial population, which is the Born rule emerging from accumulated \
evidence."
}], "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one frozen-qubit trajectory from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 " and watch ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "17", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}],
            ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"zComp", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<z = \[Rho]00 - \[Rho]11\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<one frozen-qubit record: localization by Bayes\>\""}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],

Cell["\<\
The population difference wanders under the noisy evidence and then commits \
to a pole and stays there; the \"collapse\" is the accumulation of \
log-likelihood, not a discontinuous jump.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell["\<\
3. The Purity Ride-Along: A Pure State Stays Pure in a Single Run\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is the fact that makes an ideal detector special. The coherence is not \
measured; it rides on the populations through the geometric mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],
 ", so the ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],
 " is left untouched by every update. A state that starts pure therefore \
stays exactly pure along the whole record, never leaving the surface of the \
Bloch sphere, even as its populations localize."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First confirm the invariance symbolically, and get the lossy case for free: \
check that one update, for any reading, multiplies the ride-along ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 " by exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 ", so an ideal update (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],
 ") leaves it untouched:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "r00", ",", " ", "r01", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", 
     "gt"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"r00", ",", " ", "r01"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r01", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r00"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "gt"}], 
          "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gt"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"r01", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r01", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"r00", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r00"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "r00", " ", "<", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gt", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ratio is multiplied by the same factor whatever the record says, so for \
an ideal detector it is algebraically conserved and purity is a constant of \
the single-run motion, while a lossy detector bleeds it at the fixed rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],
 "; that one factor is the mechanism behind Section 5's purity ceiling, and \
for an undriven record it will give the purity in closed form. Watch it hold \
along a record that starts pure on the equator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],
 ", while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],
 " localizes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "8", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}],
            ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"zComp", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<value\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<purity Tr[\[Rho]^2]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<ideal detector: purity pinned while z localizes\>\""}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As you may have noticed, the purity sits flat at one while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],
 " wanders to a pole: information gain alone does not decohere a single run. \
The ensemble decoheres only because different runs localize to different \
poles, which is the subject of Section 7."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell["\<\
4. Rabi Under Measurement: A Bayes Kick Between Half-Rotations\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now switch on the drive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"q", "b"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],
 " and interleave it with the measurement by the symmetric split: a half \
rotation, the Bayesian kick, another half rotation. The measurement pulls the \
state toward the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 "-poles while the field rotates it, so a single trajectory is a noisy Rabi \
oscillation whose phase slowly diffuses; a run that starts fully mixed at the \
center of the Bloch ball sharpens into that oscillation as the record accrues."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one noisy-Rabi trajectory from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],
 " and, beside it, a run that starts fully mixed and purifies:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "500"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"om", " ", "=", " ", "1."}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"uH", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"om", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"pure", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
                RowBox[{"uH", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
                "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"mixed", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "8", "]"}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
                RowBox[{"uH", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
                "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
             "/@", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "pure", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<Bloch vector\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{
            "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
             " ", "\"\<pure start from |0>: noisy Rabi\>\""}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "250"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
          "     ", 
          RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
             "/@", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "mixed", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            
            RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<Bloch vector\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{
            "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
             " ", "\"\<mixed start: purifies into oscillation\>\""}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "250"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],

Cell["\<\
The pure run oscillates and wobbles but keeps its full Bloch length, while \
the mixed run starts at the origin and swells outward into the same \
phase-locked, slowly diffusing oscillation: the record both drives and \
sharpens the state at once.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],

Cell["5. A Non-Ideal Detector: Ideality Caps the Purity", "Section",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A realistic detector loses some of the information it gathers before it \
reaches the output, and that lost information appears as an extra \
pure-dephasing factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],
 " on the coherence, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],
 ". The measurement keeps localizing at the same informational rate, but the \
coherence is now bled faster than the populations sharpen, so the state \
settles short of the surface at a steady purity set entirely by the ideality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Overlay the ensemble-averaged purity for a driven qubit measured by \
detectors of ideality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}], ",", " ", "0.7", ",", " ", "0.4"}]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 ", the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],
 " per step:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "500"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"om", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "80"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"uH", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"om", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
                RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"1000", " ", "eta"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}],
                    "]"}], ";", "\n", "          ", 
                  RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"uH", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"gm", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"1", "/", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ",
                     "tau"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
           "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.7", ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}]}], 
          "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.4", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<mean purity Tr[\[Rho]^2]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<\[Eta] = 1\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Eta] = 0.7\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<\[Eta] = 0.4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<ideality caps the steady purity\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, only the ideal detector holds the state pure; below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],
 " the purity settles onto a ceiling that drops as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],
 " drops. The mechanism is the per-step law Section 3 proved: every update \
multiplies the ride-along ratio by exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],
 ", so the ceiling sits where that steady bleed balances the localization \
that sharpens the populations. The extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],
 " is potential information dissipated inside the detector, and only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],
 " lets you monitor the wavefunction itself."
}], "Text",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Switch the drive off and the same law hands over the whole answer. Along an \
undriven record from the equator the ratio starts at one, so at every instant \
the purity is pinned to the populations, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], "=", "1", "-", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "2", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 "; confirm the identity along one lossy record:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"eta", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"gt", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gm", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ", 
        "tau"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "8", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "gt"}], 
              "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"purity", "[", "#1", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"#1", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"#1", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
                 ")"}], " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gt", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"First", "[", "#2", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
                    ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
           "\n", "      ", "traj"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The identity holds to machine precision along the whole record: with no \
drive, all the stochasticity lives in the populations, and the only thing the \
lossy detector adds is the deterministic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],
 " bleed. The drive is what breaks this closed form, trading population and \
coherence between kicks, and that is why the driven ceiling above needed an \
ensemble."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],

Cell["6. The Output Spectrum and the Factor of Four", "Section",
 CellID->485911656,ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the payoff. When the drive keeps the qubit oscillating, the Rabi motion \
modulates the very current the detector reports, so the record carries a \
coherent line at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],
 " riding on the white noise floor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],
 ". Korotkov and Averin derived the line in closed form, and its height above \
the floor is bounded: at most four times the noise in the good-oscillation \
regime ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[GreaterGreater]", "\[CapitalGamma]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],
 ", reached only for an ideal detector, and degrading as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 ". This spectrum is not just a calculation: Palacios-Laloy and co-workers \
measured exactly this Rabi line in a continuously monitored superconducting \
qubit, and read its bounded height as a Leggett-Garg (temporal Bell) test of \
macroscopic realism (Nature Physics 6, 442 (2010), arXiv:1005.3435)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->181917407,ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "+", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
         SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "2"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1906087345,ExpressionUUID->"38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Half of that four is the ordinary spectrum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 "; the other half is a purely nonclassical correlation between the detector \
noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 " and the back-action it exerts on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],
 ", which no classical harmonic signal can produce. The record we simulate \
carries both halves automatically, because the same reading that enters the \
spectrum also drives the Bayesian kick. My suggestion for the essay's \
longest-running cell: read the output first, the overlaid closed form second, \
and the input code last."
}], "Text",
 CellID->354048744,ExpressionUUID->"10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],

Cell["\<\
Before simulating, read the bound off the closed form itself. Solve it for \
its one stationary point:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->786710823,ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "om", ",", " ", "gd", ",", " ", "w"}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"D", "[", 
            RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "w"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"w", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", "w", ",", " ", 
         "Reals"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"om", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"gd", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1859374462,ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The one stationary point, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],
 ", exists only while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "<", 
   SqrtBox["2"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],
 ", a weak-damping condition the good-oscillation regime ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[GreaterGreater]", "\[CapitalGamma]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 " satisfies with room to spare. Confirm that point is a maximum:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->544914423,ExpressionUUID->"3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "om", ",", " ", "gd", ",", " ", "w"}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
          RowBox[{"w", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "<",
         " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"om", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"eta", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "gd", " ", "<", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "om"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1088734259,ExpressionUUID->"287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is, so the line has a single peak; take its height in the narrow-line \
limit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->476175344,ExpressionUUID->"440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "om", ",", " ", "gd", ",", " ", "w"}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{"s", " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"w", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gd", "^", "2"}], "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"gd", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"om", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"eta", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->201272189,ExpressionUUID->"141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The height settles at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "+", "4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],
 " only as the linewidth closes; at any finite ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "/", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 " the closed form's peak sits marginally above it, so \"at most four above \
the floor\" is a statement about the good-oscillation limit, which is where \
we now simulate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->320292756,ExpressionUUID->"321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Simulate long records in the good-oscillation regime ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[GreaterGreater]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 ", average the periodogram over an ensemble for three idealities, and \
overlay the closed form (dashed):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1146801282,ExpressionUUID->"3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"om", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "14000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "200"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"etas", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "gd", ",", " ", "sClosed", ",", " ", "spec", ",", " ", "specs"}], "}"}],
      ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gm", "/", "eta"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sClosed", "[", 
        RowBox[{"eta_", ",", " ", "w_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"spec", "[", "recs_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"half", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Quotient", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
              RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
            "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"ws", " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"2.", " ", "Pi", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"s", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], 
                   ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "half"}], "}"}]}], 
               "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"psd", " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], 
                   ")"}], "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;", " ", "half"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
                 "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "recs"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
            "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ws", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
              RowBox[{"MovingAverage", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"psd", "/", 
                 RowBox[{"Median", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"Pick", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"psd", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"ws", " ", "-", " ", "2.5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
            "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"If", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Kernels", "[", "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"LaunchKernels", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DistributeDefinitions", "[", "\"\<Global`\>\"", "]"}], ";", 
      "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"specs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"gt", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "gm"}], ")"}],
               " ", "tau"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"spec", "[", 
            RowBox[{"ParallelTable", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"recordCurrents", "[", 
               RowBox[{
               "gm", ",", " ", "tau", ",", " ", "gt", ",", " ", "om", ",", 
                " ", "nst", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"7000", " ", "+", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"1000", " ", "eta"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}]}],
                "]"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}],
          ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "etas"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "  ", 
      RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{"specs", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2.2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<angular frequency \[Omega]\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<spectral density / noise floor\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
          "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<simulated \[Eta] = 1\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<simulated \[Eta] = 0.5\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<simulated \[Eta] = 0.25\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{
          "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
           " ", "\"\<output spectrum: the coherent line and the factor of \
four\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"sClosed", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "w"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
               "w", ",", " ", "0.2", ",", " ", "2.2", ",", " ", "0.002"}], 
               "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "etas"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Thick", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], 
            "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->41202278,ExpressionUUID->"087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each simulated line sits on the closed-form Lorentzian, and the coherent \
peak climbs toward four times the floor for the ideal detector and falls off \
as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 ": the line is bounded because half of its area is the noise-backaction \
correlation, which saturates only when every bit of dephasing is \
informational. The dashed peak of the sharpest line sits slightly above its \
simulated partner; that gap is the finite frequency bins and the smoothing \
window shaving the top off a narrow peak, not physics."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124146653,ExpressionUUID->"2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],

Cell["7. Cross-Check: The Stratonovich SDE and the Ito Trap", "Section",
 CellID->1232284935,ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same physics is a Bloch-Langevin stochastic differential equation in \
the sibling essay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", " ", "vs", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Ito", "/"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 ". The Bayesian update and that Stratonovich equation must agree as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 ", and comparing them exposes the classic Ito trap. The ensemble coherence \
decays at the total rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],
 "; in the Ito form of the coherence equation that decay is the term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],
 ", which is not physical decoherence at all but the Stratonovich-to-Ito \
drift correction. In other words, the term that looks like a decoherence rate \
in the Ito equation is a bookkeeping consequence of the calculus, and \
dropping it does not remove a small correction, it removes the whole \
dephasing. Hand the Stratonovich right-hand side to a plain Ito-Euler stepper \
without that term and the coherence decays at the wrong rate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2082395230,ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact ensemble decay is one Gaussian integral away from ",
 Cell[BoxData["gaussLike"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 ", so derive it before simulating it. Average one update over the readings \
the state predicts: each population picks up its own likelihood, which \
integrates to one, while the coherence picks up the geometric mean of the \
two, whose integral is the Gaussian overlap; evaluate both, the second at the \
detector's levels and window variance:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2045146513,ExpressionUUID->"37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "a0", ",", " ", "a1", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "gm", ",",
      " ", "tau"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a0", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
             RowBox[{"a0", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
             RowBox[{"a1", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}]}], 
           "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
          "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"a0", ",", " ", "a1"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
              "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "/.", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"a0", " ", "->", " ", "i0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"a1", " ", "->", " ", "i1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"var", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gm", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"tau", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->25123057,ExpressionUUID->"2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The populations are a martingale, untouched on average by measurement \
alone, and every step multiplies the ensemble-averaged coherence by exactly \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],
 " with no small-step expansion: the dashed reference in the plot below is \
derived, not fitted, and Section 3's claim that the ensemble dephases only \
because runs localize differently is now an identity about the overlap of the \
two bells."
}], "Text",
 CellID->371825621,ExpressionUUID->"539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Overlay the ensemble coherence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],
 " from three routes started on the equator: the Bayesian update, the correct \
Ito stepper with the drift term, and the naive stepper missing it, against \
the exact decay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],
 " (dashed):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1439628390,ExpressionUUID->"09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "1500"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "bayes", ",", 
       " ", "ito", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "run"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"bayes", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", 
          "0."}], "]"}], "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ito", "[", "drift_", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "z_"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
            RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "v", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"z", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm"}], ")"}], " ", "x", " ", "xb", " ", 
             "tau"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"drift", " ", "gm", " ", "x", " ", "tau"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"z", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm"}], ")"}], " ", "xb", " ", "tau"}]}]}], 
          "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"run", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "stepper_", ",", " ", "init_", ",", " ", "read_", ",", " ", "seed_"}],
         "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"read", " ", "/@", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{"seed", " ", "+", " ", "k"}], "]"}], ";", " ", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{"stepper", ",", " ", "init", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}],
             "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n",
       "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"run", "[", 
              RowBox[{"bayes", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
                   RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], " ", 
                 "&"}], ")"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
          "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"run", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ito", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", "First", ",",
                " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"run", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ito", "[", "0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", "First", ",",
                " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        
        RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.06"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        
        RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<ensemble coherence \[LeftAngleBracket]x\
\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<Bayesian update\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Ito with +(\[CapitalDelta]I)^2/4S drift\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<naive Ito, drift dropped\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
        "   ", 
        RowBox[{
        "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
         " ", "\"\<the Ito trap: the drift correction IS the dephasing\>\""}],
         ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
            "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->497245720,ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This confirms that the Bayesian update and the correct Ito stepper both \
fall onto the exact ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 " curve, while the naive stepper never dephases at all: the missing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 " term was the entire ensemble decoherence. The Bayesian form has no \
calculus ambiguity to begin with, because it is discrete Gaussian Bayes \
between unitary half-steps; the stochastic differential equation reproduces \
it only when the Stratonovich-to-Ito drift is kept."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090726268,ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell["\<\
8. The Other Back-Action: The Phase Kick and the Second Quadrature\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->2124519200,ExpressionUUID->"41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every detector in this essay has been symmetric: a quantum point contact \
whose two output levels carry the same noise, so the correlation between the \
detector's output noise and the disturbance it feeds back to the qubit \
vanishes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],
 ". That is exactly why the back-action has been purely informational. Each \
reading squeezes the populations and slides the state along a meridian of the \
Bloch sphere, changing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 ", and nothing turns the coherence. A general detector is not so gentle: \
alongside the informational disturbance it applies a second, physical one, an \
active rotation of the coherence about the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],
 "-axis, driven by the very same record."
}], "Text",
 CellID->617350884,ExpressionUUID->"0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, there are two back-actions, and so far we have felt only \
one. Korotkov names them \"spooky\" and \"realistic\". The spooky \
(informational) back-action is the non-unitary Bayes factor we have used \
throughout: it carries no physical mechanism, it is pure information, and it \
moves the state along meridians, changing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 ". The realistic (phase) back-action is unitary: it is a genuine rotation of \
the coherence about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],
 ", along the parallels of constant latitude, and it needs a physical \
mechanism, such as the fluctuating level shift an asymmetric detector \
imprints on the qubit. For a symmetric detector the second one is switched \
off; for a general one it is not."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1357963930,ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Concretely, the coherence picks up one extra factor. Where the ideal update \
multiplied ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],
 " by the geometric mean of the two likelihoods, a general detector \
multiplies it also by a record-driven phase,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1626918454,ExpressionUUID->"67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"], " ", "\[LongRightArrow]", " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]}]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"k", "k"}], "TI"]], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", " ", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->675379980,ExpressionUUID->"233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a rotation of the coherence through an angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],
 " set by the correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 " and the integrated current ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],
 " of that step. In circuit QED this second channel is not abstract: a \
phase-preserving amplifier reports two output quadratures at once, and while \
the in-phase quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],
 " carries the informational back-action, the second quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],
 " is the one that carries the phase kick. Murch, Weber, Macklin, and Siddiqi \
made the choice between the two explicit (Nature 502, 211 (2013), \
arXiv:1305.7270): running a near-quantum-limited amplifier phase-sensitively, \
they amplified one quadrature and de-amplified the other, so the qubit felt \
only the back-action they selected. Reading the informational quadrature, \
single-shot trajectories rode a meridian of the Bloch sphere toward the \
poles; reading the phase quadrature, they rode the equator as the coherence \
turned, both tracked at a quantum efficiency of 0.49."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1331866192,ExpressionUUID->"41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because the phase kick is unitary, it never touches a single run's purity: \
the ride-along of Section 3 still holds exactly, and a pure state stays on \
the surface of the Bloch sphere. It shows up instead in the ensemble, because \
different records wind the coherence by different angles and the average of \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 " shrinks toward zero. The total ensemble dephasing rate therefore splits \
into three pieces,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1391655620,ExpressionUUID->"19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "=", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
          StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"4", 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox["informational",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["K", "TI"], "2"], 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], "4"], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox["phase",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"extra", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "environment"}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->861714746,ExpressionUUID->"6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and the fraction of that rate which is informational is precisely the \
number that fixes how far the Section 6 line rises above its noise floor: the \
peak settles at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "+", "4", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],
 " times the floor, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "\[CapitalGamma]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],
 ". In Section 6 the rise degraded as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],
 " only because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 " made ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 "; in general the rise is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],
 ", and the phase back-action pushes it down even when the detector wastes no \
information internally (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],
 "). A phase-preserving amplifier splits its dephasing evenly between the two \
quadratures, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],
 " and its coherent line can rise at most twice above the noise floor, never \
four times."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1192942815,ExpressionUUID->"34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The phase rate is one Gaussian integral away, exactly as the informational \
rate was. Average the phase factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],
 " over the readings a state at level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],
 " produces:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->556077107,ExpressionUUID->"29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "mu", ",", " ", "kk", ",", " ", "tau", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "ibar"}],
     "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
         RowBox[{"mu", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "kk", " ", "ibar", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",",
        "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ss", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"tau", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"mu", ",", " ", "kk"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
           "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ss", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tau", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"mu", ",", " ", "kk"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
        "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->15883883,ExpressionUUID->"47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The argument advances with the mean level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],
 "; read off the modulus, the ensemble dephasing the phase kick leaves behind:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->308842859,ExpressionUUID->"2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "mu", ",", " ", "kk", ",", " ", "tau", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "ibar"}],
     "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
           RowBox[{"mu", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "kk", " ", "ibar", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}],
          ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"ss", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"tau", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"mu", ",", " ", "kk"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
             "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"kk", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "ss", " ", 
        RowBox[{"tau", "/", "4"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ss", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"tau", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"mu", ",", " ", "kk"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
         "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->1108042358,ExpressionUUID->"5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The modulus decays at exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],
 " per unit time: the second piece of the dephasing split is derived from the \
same ",
 Cell[BoxData["gaussLike"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],
 " as the first, and it is pure ensemble loss, invisible in any single run. \
The general weak-measurement (Kraus) operator for a reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],
 " factorizes into a unitary times a positive part,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1009200201,ExpressionUUID->"5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "/", "2"}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]], 
      TemplateBox[{"0"},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{"0"},
       "Bra"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]], 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Ket"], 
      RowBox[{
       TemplateBox[{"1"},
        "Bra"], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->752465254,ExpressionUUID->"2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The positive square-root factor is exactly the informational Bayes update \
we built in Section 2; the unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],
 " is the phase rotation, which we quietly set to the identity by taking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],
 ". Everything in this essay so far has been the special case ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->891183881,ExpressionUUID->"196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Turn the phase kick on and watch it act. Run one record through both \
detectors from the same pure equatorial start ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],
 ", and plot the coherence in the equatorial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],
 " plane for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],
 " beside the symmetric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "056fda38-a5bc-2884-3314-dc65cc497aee"],
 " run:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->741634648,ExpressionUUID->"383c4a9f-130c-f8c1-69c4-63d9a6beca2b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.3"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "80"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kk", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"seed", " ", "=", " ", "3"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"plus", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"phaseStep", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", "kval", "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{"rho", ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"With", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"ib", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
               "       ", 
               RowBox[{"With", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"uk", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "kval", " ", "ib", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"I", " ", "kval", " ", "ib", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
                  "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
                 RowBox[{"uk", " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                   "rho", ",", " ", "ib", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "0."}], 
                   "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uk", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}],
               "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"pathK", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"Most", " ", "@*", " ", "blochVec"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", 
             "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", " ", 
               RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"phaseStep", "[", "kk", "]"}], ",", " ", "plus", ",",
                  " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"path0", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"Most", " ", "@*", " ", "blochVec"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", 
             "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", " ", 
               RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"phaseStep", "[", "0.", "]"}], ",", " ", "plus", ",",
                  " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"pathK", ",", " ", "path0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
            " ", 
           RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"\"\<Bloch x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Bloch y\>\""}], 
             "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<K \[NotEqual] 0: phase + informational\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<K = 0: informational only\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{
           "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<same record: the phase back-action winds the coherence \
about z\>\""}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"GrayLevel", "[", "0.6", "]"}], ",", " ", "Dashed", ",",
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"Circle", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1"}], 
               "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->359589406,ExpressionUUID->"7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same record that localizes the populations now also carries the \
coherence around the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],
 "-axis: the symmetric detector slides the state straight inward along a \
meridian with the phase pinned (the radial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],
 " track), while the general detector adds the parallel motion, a unitary \
turn through an angle equal to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],
 " times the integrated current (the winding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],
 " track), so every single run stays exactly as pure as before even though \
the ensemble of records now dephases faster. Turning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],
 " fully on, and letting two such detectors act at once, is where the essay \
goes next."
}], "Text",
 CellID->533832725,ExpressionUUID->"721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],

Cell["\<\
Everything up to here has been one detector on one axis. The Kraus operator \
of Section 8 is the hinge for the two generalizations that fill the rest of \
the essay: keep the single qubit but point a second detector at a different \
axis, so the two informational kicks no longer commute (Sections 9 to 15); \
then keep the single detector but let it read a joint operator on two qubits, \
so a measurement alone can entangle them (Sections 16 to 20). Both are the \
same Gaussian measurement operator, applied twice or applied to a larger \
space, and each one has now been carried out in a real superconducting-qubit \
laboratory.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->739917449,ExpressionUUID->"0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],

Cell["9. A Second Detector: A Kraus Operator for Any Axis", "Section",
 CellID->473762610,ExpressionUUID->"3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Section 8 wrote one step of the measurement as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],
 ", the phase kick times the informational Bayes factor. Keep the phase kick \
off (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],
 ", a phase-sensitive amplifier on the optimal quadrature) but stop requiring \
the measured axis to be ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],
 ": a linear detector can read any Pauli ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],
 ", with the same Gaussian informational factor, now diagonal in the \
eigenbasis of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],
 ". Point two such detectors at one qubit at once, the first on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],
 " and the second on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]", "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],
 ", an axis in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],
 "-plane at angle ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13e711b4-4d78-4d68-419c-88fe640d17b2"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fd09d86-aea1-a602-65ef-14e3cb550d68"],
 ". They emit two noisy records,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1751712322,ExpressionUUID->"2f6c0922-6605-ed68-5513-a08c13b1b7b2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Tr",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1390140890,ExpressionUUID->"2caab86a-2af9-b1b1-54a9-32344e8d039b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with independent white noises of single-sided density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", "\[CapitalGamma]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f56169e-4783-4dbb-256d-8fd872361781"],
 "; both channels are equally strong, with rate ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalGamma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b84d4d6-858d-5842-09bb-cd902c382aa8"],
 ", and ideal, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67558936-e5eb-8680-0d6a-2173939fecea"],
 ", so a step-averaged reading has window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1072dc7c-f7d5-c74e-4001-d6398261ad94"],
 " as in Part I."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1031105928,ExpressionUUID->"3462f0a3-098c-f6b3-5c11-e90da83edc99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bloch vector and purity are already defined in Part I; add the angled \
axis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04cac1af-436c-9192-2cc9-d809761ee3f8"],
 " and the Bloch length ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["r",
      FontWeight->"Bold",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63be94f2-239e-9b81-1145-0dbc5628e9eb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1410588720,ExpressionUUID->"5a3d7a71-218e-1995-0bc3-7c3b503b6bff"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", ",", " ", "rlen", ",", " ", "blochRho"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "phi", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rlen", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
    RowBox[{"blochVec", "[", "rho", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "y_", ",", " ", "z_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"x", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"y", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"z", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
   "2"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1051974278,ExpressionUUID->"3a0f2024-2f71-09ca-6a34-b98e4a045b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bloch length is one for a pure state and shrinks for a mixed one, the \
single number that says whether the two records monitor a wavefunction or \
only its blurred image; ",
 Cell[BoxData["blochRho"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "277956ac-4c9d-d338-4d07-4ff66529be02"],
 " writes the general qubit state from its Bloch coordinates, the state every \
symbolic check below runs on. For a qubit the Bloch length carries the same \
content as the purity, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        StyleBox["r",
         FontWeight->"Bold",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "178a6a52-23e4-1142-3d89-8c1c559163a8"],
 "; confirm the two agree for any qubit:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1989924844,ExpressionUUID->"52ddf811-e480-8137-02e2-f25a8d3ad01d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"purity", "[", 
       RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"rlen", "[", 
           RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
            RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", 
          "2"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", 
      " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->695529426,ExpressionUUID->"719ae17a-c654-ed44-27b9-f927f3e6b7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The identity holds, so a steady Bloch length and a steady purity are the \
same statement, which we use in Section 13. Now the operator the rest of Part \
II turns on: the informational factor for a reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62c8f42b-c628-388a-12f7-ee74f3c28ad0"],
 " of a Pauli ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36e5ffeb-8179-694d-5e9a-f6b5300c3b97"],
 ", the matrix function that multiplies each eigen-amplitude by the square \
root of its likelihood:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->767788723,ExpressionUUID->"7af061c8-c44a-ae8e-2a80-7895edfcf4d4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "kraus", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ibar_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"ibar", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], " ", "A"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->494419947,ExpressionUUID->"0d437dad-8290-de9a-3b71-74f7372aa4e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "2"], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aafc905-908a-67da-2a54-e16f213f4d20"],
 ", this is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cosh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\|01d7d9", "+", 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62016b94-8ad8-fb56-123e-82de2f52c9bc"],
 ", applied as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"M", "\[Rho]", "M"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e7c794a-82c2-56e7-3604-711437773ccd"],
 ". For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30f601cf-5001-fb68-608d-98a961b5c9b2"],
 " it is diagonal and is exactly the Part I population update in operator \
form; look at it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1581507689,ExpressionUUID->"04bc0f0b-f02f-243d-2c43-a75481db8f07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", "//",
   " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->2120100675,ExpressionUUID->"1a24bdc2-598a-1b95-4bdb-34ac583f69ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the single-axis operator is diagonal, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "705e212e-f5a4-7717-2065-b88bfc515a7d"],
 ": it scales the two amplitudes in the measured basis and leaves the \
coherence riding along. \"Exactly the Part I update in operator form\" is a \
checkable statement, so check it: conjugating any state by the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c2f5325-a3f6-c048-05d5-4a8ed5809292"],
 " operator and normalizing must reproduce ",
 Cell[BoxData["bayesUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "211ecaf2-61ee-418f-5725-e3bc179b13d5"],
 " for any reading:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->950326543,ExpressionUUID->"51e4dffc-d38f-5703-079b-d6b9e63a3a69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"r00", ",", " ", "r01", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"r00", ",", " ", "r01"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r01", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r00"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
         RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "var"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "0"}], 
         "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", "r", " ", ".", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "m", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "/", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "s", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "r00", " ", "<", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->1689126594,ExpressionUUID->"30e43b5d-74af-d0fb-609b-b3077d5ba2c1"],

Cell["\<\
The two forms agree identically, so everything Part I established, the Bayes \
localization, the ride-along, the ensemble decay, is inherited by the \
operator form. Everything below is what a second operator, diagonal in a \
different basis, does to it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1490757098,ExpressionUUID->"44d9380c-2e05-8f35-6ce6-b2564bb1d21f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the honest two-outcome draw for a general axis, sampling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36758762-649a-f7b1-5e0a-1f4c0d2cdd9b"],
 " with the Born weights ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"A", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "138e1639-4d05-8b97-41b5-886364b1d9fd"],
 " and burying the level under window noise:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->148290444,ExpressionUUID->"156728ce-0023-e03b-431c-c1a8b1d7b301"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "drawRead", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
  "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
             RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
              RowBox[{"A", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
          "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
             RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
              RowBox[{"A", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
          "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1."}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dvar", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->1707667820,ExpressionUUID->"7fc37353-2ed8-42c8-25f1-6b1d4b6d1012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each detector picks which eigenvalue to ring with the Born weights of its \
own axis, then adds Gaussian noise of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26ff5c08-e081-ff27-4e85-56559135c20d"],
 "; the two channels draw independently from the same state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->933399197,ExpressionUUID->"07c988c4-3ef2-8066-2df6-21aeba84d34c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the sampler and the operator to describe one and the same detector, two \
identities must hold. The first needs a measure on readings: take the \
Gaussian base measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "\|01d4a9", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1", "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bc0a2f3-6150-447f-79ff-3bbd10e52f45"],
 ", its constant factor chosen so that the squared kick operators resolve the \
identity and the continuum of readings is a legitimate POVM; confirm the \
resolution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->955179929,ExpressionUUID->"7ac66077-3bfa-1f18-2afe-7a31bd8f6262"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ib"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", "m"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->775067320,ExpressionUUID->"3d863d84-94ab-5643-6bbd-b4ee1d5e3ca9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The identity comes back, so the readings form a POVM over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["w", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ab8b877-e011-189c-2a47-323091a46ae6"],
 ". Second, the Born mixture ",
 Cell[BoxData["drawRead"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35eb0178-2238-e094-63e8-992257b2b2fe"],
 " samples must be exactly that POVM's predictive density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"M", "\[Rho]", "M"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0da6433d-a7a4-ba24-3b5e-5b66d256090e"],
 "; confirm the two densities agree for every state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->72268088,ExpressionUUID->"462f64f6-435d-c7dd-6fd5-7db076e9ad27"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ib", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
            RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ",
            "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ib"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", "\n", 
        "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "z"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ib"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "z"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ib"}], 
           "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ib"}], 
            "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->546416532,ExpressionUUID->"4b06bf63-5f43-ed7c-793d-374d5af7b446"],

Cell["\<\
They agree identically: the Monte-Carlo detector and the algebraic one are \
the same object, so what the ensembles below sample is exactly what the \
symbolic identities constrain.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2117784656,ExpressionUUID->"0fd1c247-21a4-d962-35ee-e4215056a848"],

Cell["10. Why the Closed Form Breaks: The Two Kicks Do Not Commute", "Section",
 CellID->853117843,ExpressionUUID->"09347675-9fce-c17b-38cc-683f1a789041"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A second detector on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c597ed5-00d9-d535-5467-779fb16dbc1f"],
 " contributes its own Gaussian operator, diagonal in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c4d8d6-27c8-a0db-0efb-d1905262f221"],
 " basis rather than the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d3801b6-8b23-0df3-74c7-98f02ed657d9"],
 " basis. To apply both over one step we multiply the two operators, and the \
order matters unless they commute. They do not, and the mismatch is the \
entire reason simultaneous non-commuting measurement is a distinct process. \
Compute the commutator of the two single-axis kicks for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09816d05-11e9-fb6e-3fbe-856fa79dc9b4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35ec423d-cde2-7917-6394-6466eb97487d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->623836386,ExpressionUUID->"05e0e9bc-56b1-1bf2-339f-00e6634469d8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
      " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], 
     " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
      " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}]}],
     "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->564394165,ExpressionUUID->"46408f14-a324-388b-6e7f-2751d6d68ad1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The commutator is nonzero and off-diagonal, so there is no basis in which \
both kicks are diagonal at once, and therefore no closed-form population \
update. Confirm the mismatch is exactly a kick about the third axis, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40213c85-9219-7c2b-71de-b5ef27ac4771"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2048244887,ExpressionUUID->"678faed4-2cca-f411-0db4-479e457cdf7b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
         RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
        " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
         RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}],
        " ", "-", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
         RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
        " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
         RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], " ", "==", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
        RowBox[{"b", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"a", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"b", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->1432457359,ExpressionUUID->"3b3cac94-919f-f08d-6ac3-45de202bc2d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two kicks fail to commute by a rotation about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "634a1270-2707-566e-1149-943a52b23cb4"],
 ", inheriting the algebra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "571f0194-b08e-3ab4-7d24-98d1c138889e"],
 " of the observables they measure. The mismatch is first order in each \
reading, so the two orderings agree as the step shrinks; but at any finite \
step the joint measurement mixes the two channels, and we must carry the full \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79764466-e076-5945-2f0e-5e4391032baf"],
 " matrix. Split the step the same way Part I split ",
 Cell[BoxData["drawCurrent"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e8dec7-14b1-519a-7c97-d7a19d4423e0"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData["bayesUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25f5c72f-3423-741a-538a-de89bdd65f60"],
 ": name the sandwiched step operator once, wrap it in a deterministic update \
for a given pair of readings, and let the step feed that update two honest \
draws:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->200346680,ExpressionUUID->"6dbbd446-5835-e39a-1b58-ce2059c1b1e0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"stepOp", ",", " ", "measureUpdateNC", ",", " ", "measureStepNC"}],
    "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stepOp", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ibz_", ",", " ", "ibp_", ",", " ", "phi_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", 
    ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"measureUpdateNC", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "rho_", ",", " ", "ibz_", ",", " ", "ibp_", ",", " ", "phi_", ",", " ", 
     "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"stepOp", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
            "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mm", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "mm", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
     ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "r1", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
    RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=",
   "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"measureUpdateNC", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"drawRead", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", 
    " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->447384324,ExpressionUUID->"6d34e655-b983-17e8-14cb-f81f38367d32"],

Cell["\<\
Because the update is now a plain function of the readings, its physicality \
can be checked once and for all rather than at one seed. Confirm that it \
keeps any qubit state trace one, and that the step operator is Hermitian, so \
conjugating by it preserves Hermiticity, for any pair of readings at any \
angle:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1438124241,ExpressionUUID->"5c435daa-0d1c-c5df-0471-54f4a4aeaf25"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", 
     " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"measureUpdateNC", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
            RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}],
          "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"stepOp", "[", 
         RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
         "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
         RowBox[{"stepOp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}],
           "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"y", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp",
            ",", " ", "phi"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->2000382747,ExpressionUUID->"21714cd0-c04e-e57a-570f-659df1f8cc40"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both hold identically: the denominator is the predictive probability of the \
reading pair, and a Hermitian sandwich keeps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74ff421b-073b-c6d4-1c85-6445b2cfac3e"],
 " Hermitian, so the general update is a legitimate quantum operation even \
though it is not a closed-form Bayes rule. One more identity does what no \
plot can. Each single-axis factor is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
     StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ebc3a74-dd7c-3fa6-6643-bc31d40e858c"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d5c93fe-a057-3a16-2b63-0abbd1e3897c"],
 " a traceless Pauli, so its determinant is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
     StyleBox["Tr",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"]}]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "487dadd0-5ed6-7873-7802-449a5b634b59"],
 "; confirm the whole sandwiched step operator is unimodular:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->902867877,ExpressionUUID->"5219761b-8a64-c9ff-0227-68452f169bc5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
       RowBox[{"stepOp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
        "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]",
          " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->1315202099,ExpressionUUID->"69346765-6d1c-e9c9-18cc-7f4f04aebb13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Since the determinant is multiplicative, the normalized update sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Tr",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["M", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c22b8c2-70f4-0562-25d1-31ac00816c48"],
 ": a pure state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04fec585-b88c-469b-2c85-dcef39392ce1"],
 ", stays exactly pure for every reading, every angle, every step. The \
great-circle walk of the next section never leaves the sphere as a matter of \
algebra, not of numerical luck."
}], "Text",
 CellID->376763343,ExpressionUUID->"7aa617d4-4041-969d-2a5d-8e9e71f5fce7"],

Cell["11. Orthogonal Axes: Collapse Becomes Diffusion", "Section",
 CellID->126027414,ExpressionUUID->"5e86e5c8-d785-1389-06bd-fc95e23061d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Point the second detector at right angles to the first, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3582ea65-851b-2569-63b1-0c4f2caf8fb3"],
 ", so the two watched axes are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e81d752-d9a7-cf7a-06be-cf1fd8539240"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6dc17641-57cc-3497-1bff-682b627e9efd"],
 ", maximally incompatible. Now each detector is forever trying to collapse \
the state onto its own axis while the other pulls it away, and neither wins: \
instead of localizing to a pole, the state performs a persistent random walk. \
On ideal detectors a pure state never leaves the surface of the Bloch sphere \
(the determinant identity of Section 10), and a mixed start is driven onto it \
as the record accrues. The other half of the great-circle claim is that the \
walk never leaves the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "647a9320-5a37-336f-0c19-0a8a5fc381b5"],
 "-plane, and that too is algebra, not luck: both measured axes lie in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57b40e76-1aa6-da65-7d4b-a0309f50a94f"],
 "-plane, so both Kraus factors are real, and a state with no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "575b10e3-003a-b957-7d78-89cdb1cc0bbd"],
 "-component can never acquire one. Confirm it for any readings at any \
angle:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->570920987,ExpressionUUID->"7c7345dd-208f-a284-2401-5c87513bf0ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",",
      " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"measureUpdateNC", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
        " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
      "0"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "x", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", 
           "phi"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->378517449,ExpressionUUID->"0121a537-2575-8479-30de-3d714c01ef43"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the sphere pinned by the determinant and the plane pinned by reality, \
the walk is confined to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f325126-465a-e19d-26c2-488073ecb3e7"],
 " great circle exactly. Run one orthogonal-measurement trajectory from the \
fully mixed center, keep it for the next plot, and watch the Bloch \
coordinates:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1671903560,ExpressionUUID->"739af998-c5c1-31b3-21b9-f0c5ec758399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "800"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xzWalk", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "4", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"measureStepNC", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            "nst"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "xzWalk", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        
        RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<z\>\""}],
           "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma])\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Bloch vector\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{
        "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
         " ", "\"\<orthogonal measurement: persistent diffusion, no \
collapse\>\""}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->1307059254,ExpressionUUID->"003becda-d908-4451-31d8-0587d8bd2ebb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aeb468a-2cc6-59e2-2ae9-5fd445732bc8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3873a668-04d7-31ac-6800-3832ad6383f6"],
 " coordinates wander over the whole range and never settle, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4156c81a-8a68-59d7-776d-e2442f1d2b3d"],
 " sits at exactly zero, as just proved: the state diffuses on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e7ab4-00f8-e339-7ea6-73feb172ce03"],
 " great circle, driven back and forth by the two competing records. There is \
no pole to fall into, so the collapse of the single-axis case is replaced by \
a walk that never ends. See the very same trajectory as a path on the sphere \
by plotting it in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b3ec616-de69-0141-3ac5-d853db1c53ab"],
 "-plane against the unit circle:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->538512558,ExpressionUUID->"7c0d57bf-7ae8-3253-2433-4ef97e8280b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xzWalk", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}], ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}], ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the same record as a walk on the xz great circle\>\""}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Circle", "[", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "380"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->824717693,ExpressionUUID->"0aaecb0d-dff0-cd78-3a55-e356d98a9442"],

Cell["\<\
The path hugs the unit circle, wandering around it without a preferred point: \
once the record has pulled the mixed start onto the surface, the two \
orthogonal detectors monitor the wavefunction perfectly and it stays pure, \
its position on the great circle left to diffuse freely. This is the \
isotropic persistent diffusion the single-basis picture has no room for.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->496527141,ExpressionUUID->"4fe4a286-576e-fd11-759b-3be06218c47b"],

Cell["\<\
12. Turning the Angle: From Collapse to Localized Diffusion to a Free Walk\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->2009363188,ExpressionUUID->"07179650-9fbb-2bc1-2d2c-081a1a4e792b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The angle ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aecd320-e31f-2936-2a93-ca8d96aa781c"],
 " between the two watched axes tunes the whole character of the motion. At \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "326b0854-5043-0b63-6268-a21e61f65649"],
 " the two detectors watch the same axis, their kicks commute, and the state \
collapses to a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d6edc53-4ce5-e0f2-4b15-d61d6491b2d8"],
 "-pole exactly as one strong measurement would. As ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45f7e4e6-4e1c-a184-738c-fdc06baef3ee"],
 " opens up, the state can no longer reach a single point, but the axes still \
leave an imprint: it localizes to regions near the two eigen-directions and \
jitters there. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70e98525-204e-6ba4-2096-1c8f51fb398e"],
 " the imprint vanishes and the walk is uniform."
}], "Text",
 CellID->55669068,ExpressionUUID->"704169dd-a4db-5005-207e-8086cd6e236f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watching this takes an ensemble of trajectories, and an ensemble is where \
stepping one trajectory at a time gets slow. It does not have to: every \
operation inside ",
 Cell[BoxData["measureStepNC"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b2d1c14-5aff-cd5f-2ad2-965e5e8b97a5"],
 ", the Born weights, the draws, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cosh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "+", 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ac11c1-6d0b-a8c0-1253-88ab04bffa2a"],
 " form of Section 9's operator, the products, the normalization, is \
arithmetic on matrix entries, and arithmetic does not care whether each entry \
holds one trajectory's number or the vector of that number across every \
trajectory. So stack the ensemble into a single array, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e7621e1-2fba-a33a-560d-b8cb4a4c0e00"],
 " density matrices as one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", "2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15938457-0322-a4d9-43a0-1e11b6d40e23"],
 " array, and advance them all in one step: entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f1ed2e3-b722-4b37-2525-cbccc2d7161d"],
 " of every matrix at once is the slice ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"rr", "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "i", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52e63e44-9d5c-26a1-029d-b02e14ee8c8b"],
 ", the matrix product is threaded over the stack, and the two random draws \
become two vector draws. One care keeps it fast: ",
 Cell[BoxData["Transpose"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e766a94-5ec6-6187-160d-83de5b7333ed"],
 " of a hand-assembled nested list comes back unpacked, so each helper \
repacks its result to keep the arithmetic on packed arrays. Encode the \
stacked step from those same ingredients, with the deterministic kick split \
out exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData["measureUpdateNC"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2eead67c-41e5-1519-56e9-c82677907c63"],
 " was:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1753574084,ExpressionUUID->"23a655ec-dad2-e192-515e-4cc9df64b3f8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "ensembleDot", ",", " ", "ensembleKraus", ",", " ", "ensembleDraw", ",", 
    " ", "ensembleKick", ",", " ", "ensembleStepNC"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "y_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Developer`ToPackedArray", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Dot", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ensembleKraus", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ib_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", 
         RowBox[{"ib", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
         RowBox[{"ib", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Developer`ToPackedArray", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"c", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"s", " ", 
              RowBox[{"A", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"s", " ", 
             RowBox[{"A", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"s", " ", 
             RowBox[{"A", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"c", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"s", " ", 
              RowBox[{"A", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
         "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ensembleDraw", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rr_", ",", " ", "A_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"pUp", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1.", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"A", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"rr", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], 
                "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"A", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"rr", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], 
                "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "          ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"A", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"rr", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], 
                "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"A", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"rr", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], 
                "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1."}], ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], 
        "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
        RowBox[{"pUp", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
          RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Length", "[", "rr", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", 
      " ", "1.", " ", "+", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dvar", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "rr", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ensembleKick", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "rr_", ",", " ", "ibz_", ",", " ", "ibp_", ",", " ", "phi_", ",", " ", 
     "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sz", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "@", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"sp", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "@", 
         RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"mz", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ensembleKraus", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ibz", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "sz", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
          "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"r2", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"mm", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                RowBox[{"mz", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"ensembleKraus", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", "sp", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
                   ",", " ", "mz"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
             "        ", 
             RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                RowBox[{"mm", ",", " ", "rr"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "mm"}], 
              "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"r2", "/", 
          RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"r2", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
            " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"r2", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
           "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ensembleStepNC", "[", 
   RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"sz", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "@", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"sp", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "@", 
        RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    
    RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ensembleKick", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ensembleDraw", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", "sz", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ensembleDraw", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", "sp", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->2038359728,ExpressionUUID->"62ef85cc-c62f-39ac-1294-1ca9f3db8bf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The step is the same symmetric split as before, the half ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d6c313b-6800-4a9b-2b13-a96509b518e1"],
 "-kick reused on both sides of the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75dfb56b-bb47-a02b-23e4-2d353ef3f371"],
 "-kick with a single draw behind it, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["UnitStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57533ce7-69d6-be0e-7d60-b5c108600554"],
 " against a vector of uniform draws replaces the one-at-a-time eigenvalue \
choice; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27c3fefb-2ee6-8038-4df0-f7a54a90d302"],
 " is symmetric, so the conjugation needs no transpose. Before trusting the \
stacked code with any physics, pin it to the code the physics was proved \
about: a stack of one state against ",
 Cell[BoxData["measureUpdateNC"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60d4995f-bb7f-b80c-10eb-11193e0b0b56"],
 ", over a grid of readings, angles, and variances:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1525364821,ExpressionUUID->"64608bbe-760c-8af3-0c1f-22f803bed8d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.6", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.1", " ", "I"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"0.1", " ", "I"}]}], ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"First", "[", 
          RowBox[{"ensembleKick", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", "rho", "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "ibz", "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "ibp", "}"}], ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
           "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"measureUpdateNC", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "rho", ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",", " ", 
           "dvar"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1.3"}], ",", " ", "0.7"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "0.4"}], ",", " ", "2.1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dvar", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1.5", ",", " ", "25."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->1535108406,ExpressionUUID->"09661063-a2cf-675e-3f1d-8a4cd77a4da4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two implementations agree at machine precision, so every identity \
Section 10 proved about the single update, trace, Hermiticity, determinant, \
the pinned ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5561d787-26b0-8d0a-031e-cee1534ad450"],
 ", transfers to the stacked run wholesale. Now run the stacked ensemble from \
the center for three angles and read, at the end of each run, how far the \
state sits from the equator, the mean of ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fea91e8-e80e-a1ed-35e9-08b589b8f337"],
 ", keyed by the angle:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1528788962,ExpressionUUID->"37725419-c8bf-c4cd-5d02-4e42e94bae17"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.03"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "250"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "200"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
        RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
              RowBox[{"100", " ", "phi"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"fin", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"ensembleStepNC", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ",
                    "ntr"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
             "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
               RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], 
                  "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], 
                  "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->1505774531,ExpressionUUID->"6eee5857-8f9d-bf63-1696-52112a290249"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2635f536-2fc9-ab3c-4fca-ed704a7df606"],
 " the mean of ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b3760e9-4a32-92b2-4acd-79b36fc4e098"],
 " is one (the state has collapsed to a pole), at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fe93a8-4ee9-5b9e-3c85-0af26a9c29e4"],
 " it drops to an intermediate value (localized but pulled toward the poles), \
and at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11cf5d11-52cc-ddbb-47f5-555b677ea781"],
 " it settles near the value a uniform point on the great circle would give, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", "\[Pi]", "\[TildeTilde]", "0.64"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ba8138a-66ce-478c-2957-8ad4137b2dd6"],
 ": the axes have stopped imprinting and the walk has gone isotropic. This is \
exactly the transition Hacohen-Gourgy and co-workers watched on a transmon \
coupled to two cavity modes, one amplifier per mode (Nature 538, 491 (2016), \
arXiv:1608.06652): as they rotated the two measured axes from parallel to \
orthogonal, the reconstructed motion passed from collapse through localized \
diffusion to a uniform walk on the sphere, precisely this smooth handover in ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CurlyPhi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35c9e6d4-f3c4-84c1-63f6-ff918676ee2b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->535490749,ExpressionUUID->"6fd66644-13e4-6fa7-15ee-782ea591358d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This stepper carries two approximations: the interleaved split of the \
kicks, and the sampling, which draws both readings from the state at the top \
of the step instead of conditioning each on the other's kick. So give Part II \
the same cross-check Part I got in Section 7, and derive the reference first. \
Averaged over its readings, one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00abf1cf-696b-3507-30a8-e8a9081f9c6d"],
 "-kick multiplies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d898fe-d35a-9eef-31e7-11bbe6ece435"],
 " by exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03dda600-4b0b-c3af-31e2-386a6ebf91f5"],
 ": weight each reading by the Section 9 base measure and integrate:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1238905205,ExpressionUUID->"4de38b79-ee67-8bee-7b90-23228b13d934"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "ib", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"mx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"mx", " ", ".", " ", 
               RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
                RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}], " ", ".", 
               " ", "mx"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ib"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
          "     ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"ib", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]",
               " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"z", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->2125008310,ExpressionUUID->"347cf1ed-0cc4-b4dc-5c03-e8b7a5761e26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is Section 7's Gaussian-overlap integral taken in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d81b9ce-3a4c-aa2a-2bbe-30a8bffef970"],
 " basis, closing with no small-step expansion, so the unconditional mean \
from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6bb9b374-9caf-337d-1946-2b3e155b9e47"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c340229-13f4-0181-15cb-a473a58153eb"],
 " must decay as exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25dfa134-0866-9bb5-53e4-397ea910e99f"],
 ". Measure the stacked ensemble's deviation from that exact value at a fixed \
time, sweeping the step from reckless to careful, keyed by the step:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1684656716,ExpressionUUID->"425139cc-45a5-cefb-726e-b0966c5194c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", "1.2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "20000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"dt", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"fin", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ensembleStepNC", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], ",",
                "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 "ntr"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
            "     ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
               " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], 
                "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", "tf"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "0.6", ",", " ", "0.3", ",", " ", "0.1", ",", " ", "0.04", ",", " ", 
       "0.02", ",", " ", "0.01"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:= ",
 CellID->2057792111,ExpressionUUID->"4d922994-f334-45bb-7ba1-c0d186c12f81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06c25578-1780-b25e-2ef2-4d22a23a00a4"],
 " of order one the deviation is a large fraction of the exact value itself: \
each \"weak\" look is nearly projective, and interleaved near-projections are \
not simultaneous monitoring. Deep inside the window the deviation shrinks as \
the step does, consistent with a bias first order in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f70617e-b140-9f95-0500-793bc0fae5ff"],
 ", and the leading source is the interleaving itself. To see it, integrate \
the sandwiched step operator against the base measure, once per reading, and \
look at what comes back:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->408837332,ExpressionUUID->"79d0371a-30a6-04e5-2fef-af4441536ecf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"stepOp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ibz"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ibp"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", "m"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:= ",
 CellID->1068510841,ExpressionUUID->"7d950d76-dd18-2b24-2baa-a533d4ad760e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sandwiched operators sum to a multiple of the identity; expand that \
prefactor in the small parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7234a9f4-3232-6781-23cb-40be47c74deb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1027032549,ExpressionUUID->"42668d78-f434-72a4-721d-2525fdc1408e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "dvar", "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "dvar"}], "]"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", ",", " ", "Infinity", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:= ",
 CellID->171792661,ExpressionUUID->"0c7cc198-0ad8-2426-3403-d8c2af528f0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It falls short of one at second order per step, so over a fixed time the \
miss accumulates to first order in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69698b1d-3dc2-3628-1f16-2347b4749d72"],
 ": the interleaved readings are not quite a POVM, and even a perfectly \
sampled interleaved step lets ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "701e1eb7-eeba-61c8-2025-97f08b4f3312"],
 " decay slightly more slowly than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e322415-281a-3695-37c1-be5f49ac9cff"],
 ". The split owns the miss; confirm the same integral with the two kicks \
applied one after the other instead:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->574949478,ExpressionUUID->"61beb272-ef15-9663-1745-343f8aa1fd49"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ibz"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "ibp"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "dvar"}], "]"}], "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], 
       " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
        "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"kraus", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
        "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ibp", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:= ",
 CellID->1664775781,ExpressionUUID->"5e8a6a96-06b4-6465-0689-83d0b3414f4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Exactly the identity: taken one after the other the two kicks form a \
legitimate POVM at any step size, and the interleaving is what buys the \
single shared ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55951090-ef25-ccfd-03aa-89dd8ad196c7"],
 "-draw at the price of a second-order miss per step. The remaining piece of \
the bias is the sampling, both readings drawn from the state at the top of \
the step rather than from the joint density of the pair. That sets the \
validity window for everything in this Part: keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53a2ca13-da2c-324e-0151-ec5cdfde8094"],
 " well below one; at the steps used here the offset sits at the percent \
level, comparable to the ensemble scatter of the plots. You are not locked \
into these choices: change the trajectory count or the step list in the sweep \
above and watch the deviation and its scatter move together."
}], "Text",
 CellID->884697794,ExpressionUUID->"5930221d-821b-4026-08cf-c44737ae130c"],

Cell["13. The Uncertainty Floor and the Purity Ceiling", "Section",
 CellID->784201795,ExpressionUUID->"76ba63e9-5df8-c241-1e5a-7ab3547290ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is a reason the state can never settle once the axes differ. For it \
to stop, both detectors would have to fall silent at the same instant: the \
state would have to be a still point for both back-actions at once. A single \
measurement has two such points, its two eigenstates; two non-commuting \
measurements share none, and the uncertainty principle is exactly the \
statement that the total measurement disturbance is bounded below by their \
commutator. For a qubit the disturbance the two channels deliver per step is \
proportional to the variance sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"], "+", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "319e51f9-a9ce-1d21-67a6-48a2c87b640b"],
 ", and because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "2"], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26f4962c-805e-a216-4e8b-087631e8f17c"],
 " for any Pauli axis each variance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "2"], "=", "1", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "313d5a7b-7caf-7acc-60c3-5c25755a4816"],
 ", so at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da78195-91be-94f0-5b5c-18df2048feda"],
 " the sum is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39c6b7ab-78e0-e73c-6ffd-2ef5789aca06"],
 ". In short, two detectors watching incompatible axes have no state they can \
both leave alone, so something is always being kicked. Confirm, for any pure \
state, that this sum can never fall below the commutator magnitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["z", "TI"]], ",", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "=", "2", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f7d0c35-7157-44bf-6502-a67f00e22e85"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193259712,ExpressionUUID->"47b49f91-c3c7-4deb-6d4b-16daf6721731"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "y", "]"}]}]}], " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"y", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"y", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"z", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:= ",
 CellID->1084903799,ExpressionUUID->"064e3005-d89e-7c03-2e75-aa6ed92b4769"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The inequality holds everywhere and, written as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{GridBox[{
        {
         StyleBox["y", "TI"]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76c2caed-aea0-13a2-1ef1-e3b6cb556188"],
 ", saturates only at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "260c3025-1fa9-9acd-4e33-a98f9a5de817"],
 ". More telling is the left side by itself: on the sphere the variance sum \
equals ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1e6c2c-0452-4134-7925-8676ade7101e"],
 ", never below one, because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2982aea8-af87-65d7-5fb1-47f5ca324f3d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19ac3a5e-0cd6-873c-4f53-bc18a560ea06"],
 " share no eigenstate and so no state can still both detectors at once. The \
walk of Section 11 lives precisely on the great circle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8690e9-968f-68b3-16bd-09b3233a3a99"],
 ", where the total disturbance sits at that minimum of one, the commutator \
bound gone slack but the kicking as inescapable as ever: the diffusion never \
stops because the disturbance cannot vanish, a consequence of the uncertainty \
principle rather than a numerical artifact."
}], "Text",
 CellID->964492758,ExpressionUUID->"2b6bc1ec-c569-bd9f-5968-d8c9ec1d07e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A real detector loses some of the information it gathers, and that loss \
caps how pure the state can be kept. With efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25f1a39a-81e0-db80-538e-3ac4379aa9ea"],
 " per channel the coherence is bled faster than the two records sharpen it, \
so the isotropic walk settles onto a mixed state whose purity sits below one, \
set entirely by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35466be2-b7a8-26dc-637d-82cfc2428c26"],
 ". The loss dephases the state about a measured axis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58bdea72-0ba3-5f4c-0842-0c3cae562596"],
 ": the part of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8cef58-e908-949c-16b3-070588a2fee6"],
 " diagonal in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0abc4047-6c7b-4886-3a44-5a21050e1aec"],
 "-basis stays, the off-diagonal part shrinks by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24e21d63-fe6b-5877-4c91-954cfb1e2b5d"],
 ". Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "2"], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "348d2737-4aeb-e3cb-5cb2-bf716e9fb111"],
 ", the diagonal-in-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2161c865-0900-0907-571e-e24fa8b5586d"],
 " part of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cadbe4b-a339-c651-6452-3014d6cdacbb"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31169419-f57b-983b-672d-0e42fc0feb01"],
 ", so the whole channel is one product with the axis; confirm the \
two-projector form and this one-product form agree for the angled axis and \
any qubit:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->242210635,ExpressionUUID->"40aa99e8-53bd-499c-70a9-10b266481be6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "phi"}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"blochRho", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "A"}], 
            ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"q", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "A"}], 
            ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"p", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "p"}], " ", "+", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"q", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "q"}]}], " ", "==",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"rho", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"A", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "A"}]}], ")"}], 
          "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[57]:= ",
 CellID->360816480,ExpressionUUID->"5d165407-aaf3-867b-0b2e-4e60ce87ed41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two projected pieces recombine into half the state plus half its \
conjugation by the axis, so the dephasing channel is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75cb8946-a0dc-0da7-23c8-2123d169578d"],
 ": the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63688a50-35e7-99e6-1117-2c1a4393ebcc"],
 "-populations ride through untouched, and what shrinks is exactly the \
information the detector gathered but failed to deliver. Add this loss to \
each channel after the stacked Bayesian kick and read the steady purity for \
three efficiencies, keyed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12187c95-2034-8b29-4238-75df51c6d673"],
 "; the purity of every trajectory at once is the elementwise product of the \
stack with its own transpose:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1505759259,ExpressionUUID->"34b193bd-0a67-a7a6-5c4e-0ae7af130d8c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "150"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ensembleStepNC", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"zB", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"N", "@", 
           RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "ntr"}], 
         "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"xB", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"N", "@", 
           RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "ntr"}], "]"}]}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
        RowBox[{"eta", ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"1.", "/", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", "1."}], ")"}], " ",
                "dt"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"deph", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", "aB"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "e"}], ")"}], " ", "rr"}], 
                    " ", "+", " ", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "e"}], ")"}], " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"aB", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", "aB"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}],
                   "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
                RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"1000", " ", "eta"}], "]"}], "]"}], ";", "\n", 
               "       ", 
               RowBox[{"With", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"fin", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Nest", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"deph", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"deph", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"step", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "zB"}], "]"}], 
                    ",", " ", "xB"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
                    "           ", 
                    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ",
                     "ntr"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                 "\n", "        ", 
                 RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"fin", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"fin", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
                    "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
                  "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.64", ",", " ", "0.36"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[58]:= ",
 CellID->1384053022,ExpressionUUID->"4fca8ec2-4b73-3b52-75c9-27ac6e0789b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The steady purity is the ceiling the efficiency allows: only the ideal \
detector holds a fully pure state, and below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "656925a1-dac3-d209-1316-bc0adf77a153"],
 " the ceiling falls, the two records no longer able to keep the state pure. \
Through the identity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        StyleBox["r",
         FontWeight->"Bold",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09e13884-5cc5-f650-3f9e-b1ee5571dcba"],
 ", this is a statement about the Bloch length: the two records feed purity \
in at a rate proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29829495-262a-abaa-5fb1-0ddf53dcf9f0"],
 ", while the information the detector fails to deliver drains it at a rate \
proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136212ad-a4c2-b9f3-4111-8bf6cd740bd9"],
 ", and the length settles where the two rates balance; we read both rates \
off the ensemble-averaged step without deriving them here, and let the \
simulated ceiling be the check. A steady, efficiency-capped Bloch length of \
exactly this kind is what the two-mode experiment reconstructed at its own \
efficiencies. The lost information is the gap between monitoring an actual \
wavefunction and monitoring only its blurred image."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1395659232,ExpressionUUID->"67f6b273-a0bf-ee61-0d8d-343cd14bb54b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The balance is quadratic in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07a2a6c0-d7ac-3784-2d51-3fade25e9dee"],
 ", so let ",
 Cell[BoxData["Solve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d29df82-54ab-6c21-24d6-d6ec5d5e370b"],
 " settle it on the physical interval: it returns a single root ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["u", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2673b224-f5d9-a24c-4e00-2b81fc6df096"],
 " between zero and one, the steady purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    StyleBox["u", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27388ee6-22a7-f122-4ec7-27c05753c008"],
 "; encode that root and confirm it is ",
 Cell[BoxData["Solve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51cd4bfd-d3fa-9dcf-07f3-62a6e58ce715"],
 "'s root:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->874592789,ExpressionUUID->"06a776cb-b9d0-3c58-2e5d-6f95386a86a2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "puritySS", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"puritySS", "[", "eta_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"4", " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"eta", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ", "eta"}]}], 
          "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "eta"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "eta"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"puritySS", "[", "eta", "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"u", " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "u"}], ")"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"2", " ", "-", " ", "u"}], ")"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"1", "/", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ",
                   "u"}]}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "u", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
               "}"}], ",", " ", "u", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
          ")"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "eta", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[59]:= ",
 CellID->1596157938,ExpressionUUID->"7641b941-63e8-8619-1e7e-312b1582ed63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["Solve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42b8cf72-fa81-ffe6-7247-e73fff35c5cc"],
 " finds exactly one root on the interval and ",
 Cell[BoxData["puritySS"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c8db7a0-3aa3-299f-44b2-2e0abf567be5"],
 " is identically that root (the discarded root has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], ">", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473593be-64fb-e664-6eca-0af80c8fcd4e"],
 ", a Bloch vector outside the sphere). The root carries the condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79a8e286-b760-8808-2f57-fbe3c21adb52"],
 "; at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "766f3dde-6e6e-8ae3-1e14-b4980b18d8c9"],
 " the drain vanishes, the balance collapses to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7acff19c-f8f8-c05b-2af4-e8d9f97292a1"],
 ", and the closed form continues through the boundary with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36bb0aa4-099e-3511-5e58-a30ea8289c7b"],
 ", the ideal detector holding the state on the sphere. Evaluate the root at \
the three efficiencies just simulated, keyed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fab4322-7f5b-c123-15a9-5a8c7aef9009"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1496122589,ExpressionUUID->"559c0528-76f1-864e-03a3-9d720285ec94"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.64", ",", " ", "0.36"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"puritySS", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.64", ",", " ", "0.36"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[60]:= ",
 CellID->1956327387,ExpressionUUID->"4c3b3e9a-7f95-6e09-75d8-b7c47a203553"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The simulated purities of the previous cell land within about a percent of \
these roots, and the residue at this ensemble size is scatter: the balance \
owns the mechanism and the whole ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b834648-1855-f17e-29b1-581299e1c044"],
 "-dependence."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1131177628,ExpressionUUID->"6aa15cf4-f328-f435-1a5f-55b186c2df1f"],

Cell["14. The Output Correlators and the Cosine at Zero Lag", "Section",
 CellID->611195905,ExpressionUUID->"1fa3178e-7287-38be-4550-8ee807338a84"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the payoff. The state itself is hard to see, but the two records ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33c53063-afff-c489-61fa-aa4cc98baed3"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08d8bcb3-70a4-55b3-38e7-35fd01513f99"],
 " are right there, and their temporal correlators carry the physics in \
closed form. Atalaya, Hacohen-Gourgy, Martin, Siddiqi, and Korotkov derived \
the self- and cross-correlators of the two output signals directly from the \
Bayesian equations and measured them on the two-mode apparatus \
(arXiv:1702.08077); for equally strong ideal channels with no extra evolution \
they are sums of two decaying exponentials with rates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "\[MinusPlus]", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20e38226-5aed-155d-5090-1b805e987fa7"],
 ". Encode the closed forms:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1202919897,ExpressionUUID->"160727ef-d1b8-0069-3e3c-bec8e04d52b3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kzzCF", ",", " ", "kzpCF"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"kzzCF", "[", 
    RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "gm_", ",", " ", "tau_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
    " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}]}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kzpCF", "[", 
   RowBox[{"phi_", ",", " ", "gm_", ",", " ", "tau_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}], " ",
       "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
     ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}], "/", "2"}], ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}], " ",
       "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "phi", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
     ")"}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[61]:= ",
 CellID->1334651244,ExpressionUUID->"261df1b1-b81e-57af-4e22-e8fb39ab3df5"],

Cell["\<\
Read the two limits these forms make vivid: the self-correlator starts at one \
and the cross-correlator starts at the cosine of the angle between the axes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->185339758,ExpressionUUID->"00ba9d2f-c328-50fc-3059-1488f6dd22c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"kzzCF", "[", 
     RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"kzpCF", "[", 
     RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[62]:= ",
 CellID->1677030473,ExpressionUUID->"02964792-f196-8b6e-32ae-5edf8020d9b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The self-correlator at zero lag is one and the cross-correlator at zero lag \
is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166d4e5f-4333-9385-3e13-601976c7e1ef"],
 ": aligned detectors (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c99ee20-d785-d362-44a6-078de231be48"],
 ") see perfectly correlated records, orthogonal detectors (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60858f89-56d8-6615-10ba-26d3636d4d7f"],
 ") see uncorrelated ones, and the cosine interpolates. In the experiment \
this ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e45545e-c429-efe4-567b-4e1bedddb5ce"],
 " was traced across eleven angles from the raw records, a purely dynamical \
readout of the angle between two incompatible measurements, obtained without \
ever reconstructing the state. Recover the closed forms from the records \
themselves: run an ensemble of angled-measurement records, form the \
ensemble-and-time-averaged two-time correlators, and overlay the closed \
forms. First a run that advances the stacked ensemble while emitting, at \
every step, the two vectors of readings that drive it, carrying a \
slow-rotation slot as the same symmetric split (held at zero until the next \
section), together with the two-time average, a pair of shifted slices \
multiplied elementwise:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->134345938,ExpressionUUID->"24564246-a2b2-7a9b-4c6e-6423d74748e1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ensembleRecordsNC", ",", " ", "corr"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ensembleRecordsNC", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "phi_", ",", " ", "omR_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "dvar_", ",", " ", 
     "nst_", ",", " ", "ntr_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"sz", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"N", "@", 
           RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"sp", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"N", "@", 
           RowBox[{"sigmaPhi", "[", "phi", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"omR", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"dt", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"uB", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Developer`ToPackedArray", "@", 
             RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
              RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"ubB", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Developer`ToPackedArray", "@", 
             RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "u", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               "ntr"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"FoldPairList", "[", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", "k"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"With", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"uB", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"rr", ",", " ", "ubB"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
               ",", "\n", "       ", 
               RowBox[{"With", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"ibz", " ", "=", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ensembleDraw", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "sz", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}],
                    ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"ibp", " ", "=", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ensembleDraw", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "sp", ",", " ", "dvar"}], 
                    "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"ibz", ",", " ", "ibp"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"uB", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ensembleDot", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"ensembleKick", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "r1", ",", " ", "ibz", ",", " ", "ibp", ",", " ", "phi", ",",
                     " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ubB"}], "]"}]}], 
                    "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             "ntr"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nst", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"corr", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a_", ",", " ", "b_", ",", " ", "j_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{";;", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "j"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"b", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "j"}], " ", ";;"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",",
      " ", "2"}], "]"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Length", "[", "a", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "a", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "j"}], ")"}]}], 
    ")"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[63]:= ",
 CellID->350820043,ExpressionUUID->"273d1382-afb1-09c0-4ec2-8aefca445b2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["FoldPairList"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39c9e52f-ed06-87fb-6ff6-fc8884b0edc1"],
 " threads the state stack forward while peeling the two reading vectors off \
at each step, so the records and the states share the very same noise, which \
is what makes the cross-correlator carry the back-action; ",
 Cell[BoxData["corr"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46be6341-4be3-06d9-6e46-7b2b6d966c23"],
 " averages the lag-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "352b8971-1d3f-d4c9-6328-213b94cbbe13"],
 " product over every trajectory and every start time at once. Now simulate \
two angles and compare with the closed form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->456450236,ExpressionUUID->"227c7e4b-1c68-aac8-5204-70159502f812"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "250"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "=", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"phis", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"taus", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nlag", "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"simCorr", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"recs", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"ensembleRecordsNC", "[", 
                RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
                 "nst", ",", " ", "ntr", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"700", " ", "+", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"100", " ", "phi"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
              "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"With", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"rz", " ", "=", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"rp", " ", "=", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], 
                "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"corr", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"rz", ",", " ", "rz", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], ",",
                    " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "nlag"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"corr", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"rz", ",", " ", "rp", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], ",",
                    " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "nlag"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
                "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "phis"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Catenate", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"taus", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"simCorr", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
                 "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"taus", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"simCorr", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
                 "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Length", "[", "phis", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}],
            ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "0.25"}], ",", " ", "1.25"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
            "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau] (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma])\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<output correlator\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<K_zz, \[Phi]=\[Pi]/4\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<K_z\[Phi], \[Phi]=\[Pi]/4\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<K_zz, \[Phi]=\[Pi]/2\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<K_z\[Phi], \[Phi]=\[Pi]/2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{
           "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<simulated records recover the closed-form correlators\>\
\""}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Evaluate", "@", 
            RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
             RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"kzzCF", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"kzpCF", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], 
                "}"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "phis"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tau", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:= ",
 CellID->1767337052,ExpressionUUID->"6cd9b5a9-dbed-51da-14e6-2cf2dd982320"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each simulated correlator tracks its closed-form curve, with the points \
scattering about it, correlated across neighbouring lags, at this ensemble \
size: the self-correlators decay from one, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4becebe3-5bfe-fac0-7993-02cd5d88c82a"],
 " cross-correlator starts near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[TildeTilde]", "0.71"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "312d182f-c6c7-5e1e-60d2-9188f3722564"],
 " and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1449d45f-8382-90b9-3c76-ce193634e283"],
 " cross-correlator starts near zero, the cosine law read straight off the \
records. The angle between the two incompatible measurements is written \
directly in how their noisy outputs correlate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1422053341,ExpressionUUID->"444f09dd-766a-dba7-6c74-a087031ca98d"],

Cell["15. A Hidden Rotation, and the Bacon-Shor Connection", "Section",
 CellID->603286833,ExpressionUUID->"79e9b65a-67eb-1624-2f96-2804119e7d0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One last use of the correlators, and one last connection. If a small \
unwanted rotation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "394df0e2-3b3f-7a44-6f72-e9ccbeca48ae"],
 " about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d3de1d4-e864-19c9-04c2-f89189116b13"],
 " is present, it breaks the symmetry between the two orderings and shows up \
only in the antisymmetrized cross-correlator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1adc8861-0296-99d3-4ae3-224bb720eb39"],
 ", which is otherwise zero. For the equally strong channels of the \
experiment the two decay rates coincide at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47f3727e-1788-b883-6d81-7438a2220ae9"],
 ", and that antisymmetrized combination reduces to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
     StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02bfa0ec-e0fe-2fa7-3244-39c9908b758d"],
 ", linear in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cc1833e-1ead-5711-24fe-1b789b583a7b"],
 " for a slow rotation. The rotation slot in ",
 Cell[BoxData["ensembleRecordsNC"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cb4236e-91b2-9328-644b-bb482044fe72"],
 " was built for this moment: simulate at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CurlyPhi]", "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "631da35c-735e-7e3b-1122-3b0606eb4501"],
 " with a rotation below the measurement rate, form the antisymmetrized \
cross-correlator, and overlay the closed form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1349832744,ExpressionUUID->"44b7daea-ed84-b50e-6c4c-d3b784361c54"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "250"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "2000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "=", " ", "100"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"omR", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"phi", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"taus", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nlag", "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"recs", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ensembleRecordsNC", "[", 
          RowBox[{"phi", ",", " ", "omR", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1.", "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "nst", ",",
            " ", "ntr", ",", " ", "400"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"rz", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
             RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"rp", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
             RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}],
          ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"taus", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"corr", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"rz", ",", " ", "rp", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], " ",
                    "-", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"corr", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"rp", ",", " ", "rz", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}]}], ",",
                   " ", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "nlag"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
              "]"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"-", "0.7"}], ",", " ", "0.9"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
              "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               
               RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau] (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma])\>\"", ",",
                 " ", "\"\<K_z\[Phi] - K_\[Phi]z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
             "      ", 
             RowBox[{
             "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
              " ", "\"\<the antisymmetrized cross-correlator reads the hidden \
rotation\>\""}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n",
            "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "phi", "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", "tau"}], "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
               RowBox[{"omR", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"tau", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"nlag", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
               RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
          "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[65]:= ",
 CellID->16034565,ExpressionUUID->"39f2334d-24de-3dcb-6f81-ab174d688711"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The simulated difference rises from zero, follows the dashed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "~"], 
     StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ec600b7-0050-8550-46fd-99f1b1eaefba"],
 " through its maximum, and decays with the correlation time; the points \
scatter about the curve at this ensemble size, and the scatter is correlated \
across neighbouring lags, so a stretch of them can wander off together while \
the residuals average to zero. A rotation with no visible trace in either \
record alone stands out cleanly in the ordering asymmetry of the two records. \
This is how Atalaya and co-workers read a residual Rabi frequency of 12 kHz, \
some three thousand times below the 40 MHz drive, out of the records of the \
two-mode experiment."
}], "Text",
 CellID->344152329,ExpressionUUID->"33bfe66e-cd59-d601-6144-f84be4edbd6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The whole construction has a direct afterlife in error correction, and it \
is the subject of a paper of my own (Atalaya, Bahrami, Pryadko, Korotkov, \
arXiv:1612.02096). A four-qubit Bacon-Shor code measures four two-qubit gauge \
operators continuously; in the code space the four-qubit state stays ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["z", "TI"], "+"}]},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["z", "TI"], "-"}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a3ee8c1-8740-e1ad-1bc5-01ab32fab3f7"],
 ", so the measurement drives a single spare degree of freedom, a gauge \
qubit, while leaving the logical qubit untouched. In that two-dimensional \
subspace the two ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33885b0f-111a-0c54-6188-5369a0af56be"],
 "-type gauge operators are each a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c9080a8-67dd-9047-04af-19f21269e2ad"],
 "-measurement of the gauge qubit and the two ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2abc9d06-0494-496b-5a43-1560ad211bb1"],
 "-type ones are each an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43e301a0-76bb-1057-7190-980a034e62bd"],
 "-measurement, so the gauge qubit is watched along two orthogonal axes at \
once, exactly the doubly-watched qubit of this Part: it diffuses on a great \
circle while the logical qubit rides along. The error syndrome is then read \
not from a projective parity but from the time-averaged cross-correlators of \
Section 14, which for the ideal gauge qubit take the two-time form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ae06f2b-7109-3ba5-4a9f-877500bd898f"],
 " with same-time value one; a single-qubit error moves the state into a \
subspace where a cross-correlator flips sign, and continuous monitoring \
performs about as well as projective syndrome extraction once the collapse \
time is roughly an order of magnitude shorter than the projective measurement \
period. The one-qubit cross-correlator we pulled out of simulated noise is, \
in that setting, a continuously monitored error check."
}], "Text",
 CellID->622383932,ExpressionUUID->"0856a555-3f58-6085-386d-3d1fbaed32ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The other generalization keeps a single detector but gives it two qubits to \
watch at once. If the detector is built so it cannot tell ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71eecbe3-9be0-9ba6-2795-e2cd1d9ae98c"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "59070895-187c-42ea-0f3c-a1df99091030"],
 ", the same Bayes kick that localized one qubit now entangles two, with an \
odd-parity coherence riding along exactly as the single-qubit coherence did \
in Part I."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2102744249,ExpressionUUID->"189fe470-6cd8-7cf4-48a4-fe3a056d46de"],

Cell["16. From One Qubit to Two: The Half-Parity Meter", "Section",
 CellID->565659401,ExpressionUUID->"04ed2843-d86c-272a-2c92-c22cd91e8a70"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two qubits, remote and never coupled, are read by a single probe that \
reflects off both, so its output records the pair. In the computational basis \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"00"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"01"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"10"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"11"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d9e217-b7c7-416b-20e6-0450c27213b1"],
 " the probe is engineered so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29221b72-bc55-8ef4-58d1-933c35e1d4de"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41172bde-c012-830e-772c-c29bf1a4ee54"],
 " shift it by the same amount: a half-parity meter, sorting the four states \
into three bins, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dd84232-0c35-660d-6bf8-647ca5c04d57"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5558c8fc-3d33-9e90-0367-e1a6b4c7e4fa"],
 ", and the odd pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"01"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"10"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53291d47-a111-bd44-02d6-9520d0a507ae"],
 ", never resolving which of the two odd states it holds. The window-averaged \
reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14460f59-6b0f-818e-3c7d-a7030ebbd3d4"],
 " is Gaussian about a center that takes three values, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6afe19ed-5a5e-331e-1a85-90b75fe89e64"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "142f588d-e120-bc70-3dd5-51d690da075a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "029948d8-232c-2201-32a7-618256d9716b"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1b5b6f-b43d-594b-7939-53493dc82b91"],
 ", and zero for both odd states. The reading carries white noise of \
single-sided density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32f703b9-71e1-95eb-628c-9ae30795ff31"],
 ", so a window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c860bbc-8d1f-f590-34bd-a2e624abdffa"],
 " leaves a Gaussian of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bab88a0-6539-d521-49a8-210a0ccdbc0b"],
 " exactly as in Part I, and the measurement strength is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74b37722-3fdc-1a4f-1c41-6e8cba696895"],
 ", the two-qubit counterpart of the rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31781dc2-1028-33d4-6707-94aca1c2813e"],
 "; one extra rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2148b02c-d62e-5336-5777-2989e3db3e1c"],
 " carries whatever dephasing survives inside the odd subspace. With the \
fast-damping off-diagonal elements dropped, the state is the X-state, five \
appreciable numbers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "5"], "}", "=", "{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"00", ",", "00"}]]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"11", ",", "11"}]], ",", 
   RowBox[{GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "183293a6-0d60-7813-49c1-0a00a4154b79"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->561487989,ExpressionUUID->"61e1f3c1-eae0-3799-179e-eaaa8e9a9de3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Encode the three-center Gaussian likelihoods for a reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20bddc2d-650e-8031-5042-d6770cb8d31b"],
 " and the concurrence of an X-state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2021628840,ExpressionUUID->"7a437910-f355-55ba-2a71-715d86e03f80"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"likelis", ",", " ", "concurrence"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"likelis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"v_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "dvar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "dvv"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
           "dvv"}], "}"}], " ", "-", " ", "v"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"concurrence", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[66]:= ",
 CellID->41425461,ExpressionUUID->"49429438-4a3e-974e-7f71-0e626fc8fd94"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The concurrence runs from zero for a separable or classically mixed state \
to one for a Bell state, set by a race: the odd-parity coherence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "5"], "=", GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07e2168c-1726-1a27-2d91-8fd6a2d3690d"],
 " pulling it up against the geometric mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "4"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3540c51c-f580-c338-637f-dd59fc3aae02"],
 " of the two even populations pulling it down. This is the very quantity the \
remote-entanglement experiment of Section 20 reports."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208764476,ExpressionUUID->"684f0173-fe99-1571-1874-993cfb2c7c5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That two-line formula is the Wootters concurrence specialized to the \
X-state, and it is worth seeing it come out. Wootters' construction takes the \
square roots of the eigenvalues of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e32c5a8-aee9-5273-17c1-dcf5ca9c2159"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "*"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "607492e2-157b-ba0c-100b-0bcc9c0f0956"],
 ", sorts them, and subtracts the rest from the largest; compute those roots \
for a general X-state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1584634344,ExpressionUUID->"7781757c-388d-abb9-1dbf-6d26b939f983"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x1", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "x4", ",", " ", "x5"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"xr", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"x1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}],
           ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x5", ",", " ", "0"}], 
           "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "x5", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "0"}], 
           "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "x4"}], 
           "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"sy", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
         RowBox[{"xr", " ", ".", " ", "sy", " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "xr", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "sy"}], "]"}],
         "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x2", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x3", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x4", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x5", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[67]:= ",
 CellID->35679398,ExpressionUUID->"566e7348-207a-dc95-7e16-6b12510ca6ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four roots pair up: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "4"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39672ae7-82f4-b353-6f1c-c3c1368601b9"],
 " twice from the even block, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"]}]], "\[PlusMinus]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "5"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c48aba4-6f27-6a39-3477-420e0ad23903"],
 " from the odd block (the last two entries are those squares under the \
root). Two orderings put the odd block on top. First, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "5"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f62374d-f3df-131c-5511-af16866a7e66"],
 ", the positivity of the odd block, preserved because the ride-along ratio \
never grows. Second, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "4"]}]], "\[LessEqual]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "455ea632-3d4d-f0d3-7365-387cb4f9c239"],
 ": the even centers sit a full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "v"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f0fb95c-030e-c889-4534-3106b6b89ad3"],
 " from the odd ones, so every reading multiplies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "4"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16268eae-a572-7912-3fdd-270bcc074878"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
     StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "346a0e1a-2221-987e-5c69-a04457d5eb44"],
 ", and the meter starts the two products equal; Section 17 proves both step \
laws. Under those two orderings, Wootters' combination, twice the largest \
root minus their total, must collapse to the two-line formula; confirm the \
telescoping:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1113372800,ExpressionUUID->"366be24c-537a-43bb-5e68-0416660f1181"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x1", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "x4", ",", " ", "x5"}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"lam", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "x5"}], ",", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "x5"}]}], "}"}]}],
       "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Max", "[", "lam", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", "lam", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"x5", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x2", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x3", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x4", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x5", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x5", " ", "<=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], " ", "<=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[68]:= ",
 CellID->969867355,ExpressionUUID->"501b1457-1a1d-907b-0038-8e119fa9e341"],

Cell["\<\
The identity holds on the whole ordered region: the race between the odd \
coherence and the even populations is the full Wootters concurrence on every \
state this meter can produce.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1210037699,ExpressionUUID->"291c68e0-f532-6cdd-5f23-81cdfcc73627"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the update, the single-qubit Bayes kick of Part I one level up: each of \
the four populations picks up its likelihood and renormalizes, and the \
odd-parity coherence rides on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "3"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c29c458-c353-7b98-05d6-de05f6e649e2"],
 ", the geometric mean of the two likelihoods of the states it links, with \
the extra dephasing factor. Split it as before, the deterministic update for \
a given reading and the honest step that draws the reading from the mixture \
the state predicts:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1239892393,ExpressionUUID->"6e1a2d6a-d2ad-c32a-1639-c537e759ae70"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"twoQubitUpdate", ",", " ", "twoQubitStep"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoQubitUpdate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "x_", ",", " ", "v_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "dvar_", ",", " ", 
     "gt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"likelis", "[", 
        RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"p", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"p", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"p", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        "p"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoQubitStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "gt_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], 
    "]"}], "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"twoQubitUpdate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "dvv"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
           "dvv"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dvar", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "gt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[69]:= ",
 CellID->1498748757,ExpressionUUID->"6eb5612b-2266-f0f1-164b-79755710c2db"],

Cell["\<\
That is the entire integrator: draw which bin the record leans toward with \
the current populations as weights, bury it under window noise, and fold the \
reading back into the five numbers, the four populations by classical Bayes \
and the odd coherence by the geometric-mean ride-along.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1701544389,ExpressionUUID->"1f4b4965-e043-b514-4549-614e91f71c7e"],

Cell["17. The Odd-Parity Coherence Rides Along", "Section",
 CellID->1682415361,ExpressionUUID->"5bf36e21-2d79-2b6f-0980-878b440c79b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The whole entangling mechanism is the purity ride-along of Section 3 \
promoted to the odd-parity subspace. There, because the coherence multiplied \
by the geometric mean of the two population likelihoods, the ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fe9f85b-1ce6-27f0-1596-f20594908dda"],
 " was untouched by every ideal update, so a pure state stayed pure. Here the \
same ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"01", ",", "01"}]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"10", ",", "10"}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3eadea9f-7d43-757d-6652-03d974f65c47"],
 " is untouched, so a coherent superposition inside the odd subspace stays \
coherent while the meter localizes the pair into it. Confirm three step laws \
on the update itself, for any reading and any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68be2dd2-eea3-f2cb-1845-c49f8b57c011"],
 ": the four populations keep summing to one, the ride-along ratio picks up \
exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[CapitalDelta]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1279eb8d-ef8a-5dbb-4206-02d68a3f2781"],
 " (Section 3's law, one level up), and the even-to-odd population product \
falls by exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6afb4307-9f81-9d1b-1a99-5b611a35e461"],
 ", the ordering Section 16's telescoping rests on:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1697357464,ExpressionUUID->"2e902be9-4fb4-3e90-56af-c2b36a4684fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "x1", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "x4", ",", " ", "x5", ",",
      " ", "v", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "gt"}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"twoQubitUpdate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "x1", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "x4", ",", " ", 
           "x5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar", ",",
          " ", "gt"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{"u", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==",
           " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"u", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gt"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"x5", "^", "2"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"u", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", 
              RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], "/", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], ")"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"x2", " ", "x3"}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x2", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x3", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x4", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x5", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
           "x1", " ", "+", " ", "x2", " ", "+", " ", "x3", " ", "+", " ", 
            "x4"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "dvv"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
           "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gt", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[70]:= ",
 CellID->1540797058,ExpressionUUID->"46e8ad28-93a4-355d-6e97-457226569fa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three hold identically: the update is trace-preserving, the ratio is \
conserved for an ideal meter and bled at the fixed rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43090fa7-5002-8b65-7136-a60161b4d64f"],
 " for a lossy one, whatever the record says, and the even product drains \
steadily against the odd one. So the odd-parity coherence rides its two \
populations exactly as a single qubit's coherence rides its own, which is why \
a measurement that only sorts the pair into the odd bin leaves a fully \
coherent Bell state rather than a classical mixture of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d6689b0-bbf9-a698-3b1d-20fa3d8d0ce2"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ac87485-b214-a6e0-7ac8-6deec7a60cca"],
 ". Entanglement here is not created by any interaction; it is the coherence \
already present surviving the localization, because the meter cannot look \
inside the subspace it is projecting onto."
}], "Text",
 CellID->768596373,ExpressionUUID->"56e1d4b5-6b25-2976-7e9e-cdff0ed0785c"],

Cell["18. One Record Steered into a Bell State", "Section",
 CellID->1985169054,ExpressionUUID->"2e41722a-1026-02f0-567f-7474a1d350da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start the pair in a product of equal superpositions, so all four \
populations are one quarter and the odd coherence is one quarter. The meter \
sorts each record into one of three bins: if the record leans toward ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aacec8a-85e6-bbaa-1a53-05d4339009f0"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c51a735-fee5-6802-446e-3f7efa903b68"],
 " the pair collapses toward the product state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e54a15d-ecde-9aa9-066b-39068568e8f3"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27fb6428-ecec-27d4-4d99-7e75849e8d3e"],
 " and the odd populations drain away; if it stays near zero the pair is \
steered into the odd subspace, where the surviving coherence makes it the \
Bell state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"01"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"10"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51f5ca74-88a2-9d2c-078a-ec3e2954e476"],
 ". Watch one record that lands in the odd bin, tracking its concurrence, the \
two even populations, and the total odd population:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->770675313,ExpressionUUID->"1154648e-ef0b-aa2b-476c-7deb8abff971"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "0.15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "4", "]"}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"twoQubitStep", "[", 
             RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"gam", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
             "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",",
               " ", "0.25"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"concurrence", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
          "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<concurrence\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Rho]00,00\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<\[Rho]11,11\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<odd population\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of measurement time)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<value\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<one record steered into the entangled subspace\>\""}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[71]:= ",
 CellID->846554368,ExpressionUUID->"4c057904-8649-af2b-743b-716e33fdf271"],

Cell["\<\
The two even populations drain toward zero while the odd population fills \
toward one, and the concurrence climbs and then eases back: the record has \
projected the pair into the odd subspace and the surviving coherence has \
become genuine entanglement. A different seed would drain the odd population \
instead and collapse to a product state with zero concurrence; the outcome is \
stochastic, set by which bin the noisy record favors, with the bin \
probabilities equal to the initial populations, the Born rule again.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1952818843,ExpressionUUID->"2baf9433-2e90-ebaf-5954-0e7d4b2ab9f5"],

Cell["19. The Closed-Form Concurrence Ceiling", "Section",
 CellID->599175116,ExpressionUUID->"340e6ec8-e38f-b030-5c35-8795963b031a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How entangled can a record make the pair, and how does that depend on when \
we look? The key premise is that the whole X-state is fixed by the running \
readout, and it follows from how Gaussian likelihoods compose. Before its \
normalization the update just multiplies the five numbers by the five \
per-reading factors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]}], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "3"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "4"], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], "3"]}]], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64bff79f-1679-3ebc-0c44-eed9a30d8486"],
 ", so two steps multiply by the product of two factor sets; confirm that \
product equals the factor set at the averaged reading with half the variance, \
up to one common constant, by showing the elementwise ratio of the two is the \
same in every slot:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1234886004,ExpressionUUID->"126dc52b-3dd5-bd31-4212-dd75b461041b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "v2", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "}"}], 
   ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"fac", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "dv"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"likelis", "[", 
              RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dv"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
           ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"p", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"p", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{"p", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Equal", " ", "@@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"fac", "[", 
           RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"fac", "[", 
            RowBox[{"v2", ",", " ", "dvar"}], "]"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"fac", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"v1", " ", "+", " ", "v2"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{"dvar", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dvar", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"v1", ",", " ", "v2", ",", " ", "dvv"}], "}"}], " ", "\[Element]",
            " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:= ",
 CellID->1955603644,ExpressionUUID->"28023c0b-10a3-7000-5831-b655a156436a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ratio is slot-independent, and a common constant dies in the \
normalization: two steps at readings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f1b960d-0301-b7cd-7538-0857b6b51d17"],
 " are one step at their average with half the variance, so by induction the \
state after any record depends on it only through the running mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "268b8fe7-2cf2-fa64-4e88-26c14484c94e"],
 ", with the dephasing factors multiplying up on their own. The concurrence \
at any time is therefore a definite function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41763b34-5a53-ec31-770d-b37e5fe7b71b"],
 ", and it is largest for the record that sits exactly at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d61c4f4-c0fb-847a-0b1e-ddb1f08fef40"],
 ", the most balanced odd-bin outcome. That most-fortunate concurrence is a \
closed form, given by the same quantum-Bayesian analysis the experiment of \
Section 20 is analyzed with: a race between the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72fe9a0c-0c49-239f-2285-1c56a5fc71e5"],
 " that erodes the coherence and the measurement rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14bcbead-0cb8-f132-3c43-37f7a532c018"],
 " that first builds and then over-localizes it. Encode the maximum \
concurrence and the concurrence-readout relation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->529524776,ExpressionUUID->"4a015340-38cc-91ca-7a3f-4b2ab97ee310"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"cmaxCF", ",", " ", "cOfVCF"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gam_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "t_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "gam"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"cOfVCF", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "gam_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "vt_", ",", " ", 
    "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "gam"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "vt", " ", "dvv", " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", "^", "2"}]}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"t", "/", "ss"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:= ",
 CellID->186212144,ExpressionUUID->"44807b7f-366d-41a7-6cb0-73394318138d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Show that the concurrence-readout relation is largest at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56b5d630-2397-dc8b-7e4a-c87a5623a6d1"],
 " and equals the closed-form ceiling there:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->284725946,ExpressionUUID->"066e8396-42fa-b64f-2e15-1ad0768c1c95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"cOfVCF", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "t"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"D", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"cOfVCF", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "vt", ",", " ", 
           "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "vt"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"vt", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], 
    "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[74]:= ",
 CellID->1006536905,ExpressionUUID->"0fee4e15-659c-ade9-3596-605f0c2ef733"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both are true: the concurrence is stationary in the readout at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f99faa1-7599-adaa-15a6-f30b7c2df7f0"],
 " and the value there is the ceiling, because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["cosh",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c80f068-193e-1d5a-14bf-ea3298cb67a0"],
 " is smallest at zero and sits in the denominator. No record, however lucky, \
can beat the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77601adb-bf25-4789-1d1f-93853ad02dd3"],
 " outcome."
}], "Text",
 CellID->207506748,ExpressionUUID->"48b830c7-d270-6a57-7847-a9a0e70538bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the payoff, and the five-number update stacks over an ensemble exactly \
as the two-axis step did: the state becomes an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62f1d7f5-6807-0c72-128e-cebf09b25758"],
 " array, the bin draw becomes one vector of uniform draws sorted by two ",
 Cell[BoxData["UnitStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e2af966-75ba-f15e-4629-f1407c4cc3a4"],
 " thresholds, and the two odd centers coincide, so the geometric mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "3"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcb302b-9e92-9019-25c8-aa751b24e363"],
 " is simply the shared zero-center likelihood. Encode the stacked run:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1146295856,ExpressionUUID->"361ba0ac-b25b-03c3-5e38-3909c7ee5129"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"twoQubitKick", ",", " ", "twoQubitEnsemble"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoQubitKick", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "xx_", ",", " ", "v_", ",", " ", "dvv_", ",", " ", "dvar_", ",", " ", 
     "e_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"pm", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"v", " ", "+", " ", "dvv"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"pz", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{"v", "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"pp", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"v", " ", "-", " ", "dvv"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dvar"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pm"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pz"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pz"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pp"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pz", " ", 
          "e"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "/", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pm"}], " ", "+",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
         "pz"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "pp"}]}], 
       ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twoQubitEnsemble", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "dvv_", ",", " ", "ss_", ",", " ", "gt_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", 
    "ntr_", ",", " ", "nst_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dvar", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ss", "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"e", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"NestList", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"xx", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"xx", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
                 " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
              
              RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
                RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Length", "[", "xx", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
            "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"twoQubitKick", "[", 
             RowBox[{"xx", ",", "\n", "       ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"dvv", " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"u", " ", "-", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"w", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", 
                    " ", 
                    RowBox[{"w", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", 
                    " ", 
                    RowBox[{"w", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
                  " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"w", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", 
                    " ", "u"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "        ", 
               
               RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dvar", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Length", "[", "xx", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
              "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", "e"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
         "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
           "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", " ", "0.25", ",", 
            " ", "0.25"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "ntr"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "nst"}],
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[75]:= ",
 CellID->438365529,ExpressionUUID->"36c5768f-9366-0c29-5efb-6fe926135773"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One uniform draw per trajectory picks the bin, falling below the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcd6d4-594a-1482-7183-cf9e58ff7ee8"],
 " weight or clearing everything but the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4719bc21-ede2-73f0-6d26-358a8b9741da"],
 " weight, the drawn center is buried under the window noise, and the five \
columns then update elementwise, the same Bayes-and-ride-along arithmetic \
acting on the whole ensemble at once. Pin the stacked kick to the update the \
symbolic checks ran on, a stack of one state over a grid of readings, \
strengths, and variances:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->174000849,ExpressionUUID->"71a147e0-ad25-39c0-275f-5ecdc4d18b2a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "0.21", ",", " ", "0.34", ",", " ", "0.19", ",", " ", "0.26", ",", " ", 
       "0.24"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"First", "[", 
          RowBox[{"twoQubitKick", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", "x", "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "v", "}"}], ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
             RowBox[{"-", "0.003"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{"twoQubitUpdate", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "x", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "dvar", ",", " ", 
           "0.003"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1.2"}], ",", " ", "0.1", ",", " ", "0.9"}], "}"}]}], 
       "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.7", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"dvar", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2.", ",", " ", "50."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[76]:= ",
 CellID->766726627,ExpressionUUID->"0d94734f-f5fd-5b1e-3bac-6b2883882664"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Agreement at machine precision again: the trace, ride-along, product-drain, \
and composition laws proved for ",
 Cell[BoxData["twoQubitUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a66d044-93ea-cfa5-7a1d-ca2e259c958f"],
 " are properties of the stacked run as well. Run it from the product start \
and plot every trajectory's concurrence, one ",
 Cell[BoxData["Ramp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08e3a6ae-198b-2f89-3890-3f08983e75d3"],
 " over the whole stack, against the closed-form ceiling:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1506609767,ExpressionUUID->"07ff9e3d-196e-b566-2d84-106798181c4c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "0.15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "60"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"twoQubitEnsemble", "[", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gam", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "ntr", ",", 
          " ", "nst", ",", " ", "900"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"cmat", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Ramp", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "All", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
            " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}],
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"traj", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "All", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], 
               "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "cmat", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.35", "]"}], ",", " ", "Gray"}], 
             "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0.45"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of measurement time)\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<concurrence\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{
           "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<records press against the closed-form ceiling\>\""}], ",",
            " ", 
           RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "500"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], 
            "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"nst", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "Thick", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], 
             "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[77]:= ",
 CellID->281363281,ExpressionUUID->"7611561e-6aa4-cbf1-1e2f-48580f5699db"],

Cell["\<\
Every trajectory stays below the dashed ceiling, and the luckiest ones ride \
right along it: the closed-form maximum concurrence is exactly the sharp \
cutoff of the simulated distribution, recovered from records without ever \
imposing it. The ceiling rises from zero as the measurement builds coherence \
into concurrence, peaks, and then decays as continued localization and the \
extra dephasing win, so there is an optimal moment to stop measuring. Look at \
where the trajectories end up, at a fixed late time, across a large ensemble:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1615544595,ExpressionUUID->"6d91ad73-9dce-768e-1bae-453d147b5cd4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gam", " ", "=", " ", "0.15"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "2000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"fin", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "[", 
        RowBox[{"twoQubitEnsemble", "[", 
         RowBox[{"dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gam", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "ntr", ",", 
          " ", "nst", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Ramp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"fin", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
         "]"}]}], ",", " ", "40", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<final concurrence\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<counts\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<bimodal: a spike at zero and a peak beneath the \
ceiling\>\""}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[78]:= ",
 CellID->1805673747,ExpressionUUID->"6bff65fb-5d0a-196c-1985-7ca554bf6bb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The distribution is bimodal: a tall spike at zero concurrence from the \
records that collapsed to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e58ca76-8595-5ac4-0667-ec302c20282e"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08a91809-3406-7705-3856-9253bdb35a6f"],
 ", and a separate peak of entangled outcomes that pushes up against, but \
never past, the ceiling. The two peaks are the two fates of the pair, a \
product state or the Bell subspace, and the gap between them is why the \
measurement must be conditioned, kept only when the record lands in the odd \
bin."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1547520620,ExpressionUUID->"47ee4125-d524-d464-6d96-588edcd6bf4e"],

Cell["20. What Sets the Ceiling, and the Remote-Qubit Experiment", "Section",
 CellID->858350929,ExpressionUUID->"1a0bea5a-c3ff-c671-4a08-0c07f58bad5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The height of the ceiling is a trade-off between the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d2ec88d-5e53-28f6-54d5-e1d75be67adc"],
 " and the measurement rate. A slow, clean measurement builds coherence into \
concurrence before losing it; a noisy or lossy one erodes the coherence \
faster than it can localize the pair, and the peak concurrence drops. The \
trade-off is already written in the ceiling's three limits: a perfectly clean \
meter, long times, and short times:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2138894257,ExpressionUUID->"230fc3bf-d3e5-5aa5-5134-daf8e590288f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"dvv", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ss", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"t", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], 
        "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"gam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"dvv", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ss", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", "t"}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[79]:= ",
 CellID->1941039383,ExpressionUUID->"0c6e076f-8b93-3c10-3415-9f492e27877a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A clean meter's ceiling is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["tanh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29094997-c9cb-f733-5f37-60d0e87fda19"],
 ", climbing monotonically to a full Bell state; any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "284fc6fb-b6ce-6422-5874-dfa4c37b4f08"],
 " sends the ceiling to zero at long times; and the short-time slope is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cad16aa-0a89-b805-3452-8ff4af3d0b6f"],
 ", so the concurrence rises at all only when the measurement outruns the \
loss, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "2"], ">", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5640583a-c911-1fe8-7e70-5267e8a46532"],
 ". Between the rising start and the dying tail sits a peak; read it for \
three values of the extra dephasing, keyed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6944803a-8297-e066-1f7b-1a643723b34c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1670620029,ExpressionUUID->"7e9e495e-a796-7cd0-26a6-611bd223463a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dvv", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ss", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "800"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
        RowBox[{"cmaxCF", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gam", ",", " ", "dvv", ",", " ", "ss", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", "nst", "]"}], " ", "dt"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0.05", ",", " ", "0.15", ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[80]:= ",
 CellID->588214459,ExpressionUUID->"534f7e63-03c8-ee33-0175-704db662b519"],

Cell["\<\
The peak concurrence falls as the extra dephasing grows: a nearly ideal \
channel reaches deep into the entangled regime, while a lossy one barely \
leaves the separable one. This is exactly the trade-off that capped the first \
remote-entanglement experiment (Roch, Schwartz, Motzoi, Macklin, Vijay, \
Eddins, Korotkov, Whaley, Sarovar, Siddiqi, Phys. Rev. Lett. 112, 170501 \
(2014), arXiv:1402.1868), where two transmons joined by 1.3 meters of coaxial \
cable and a shared probe reached a peak concurrence of 0.35 at a measurement \
efficiency near 0.4, before intrinsic dephasing and the finite efficiency of \
the amplifier stopped the climb; with better hardware the same analysis \
projects about 0.7.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1759496502,ExpressionUUID->"3b07ad27-9e6a-154b-693c-44811b1f7f91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The update we ran is the same one that experiment is analyzed with, and it \
says so explicitly, confirming the validity of the quantum-Bayesian formalism \
for a cascaded system. Two qubits in separate cavities, probed in sequence so \
the signal reflects off one and then the other, are a cascaded system whose \
joint measurement is exactly this half-parity meter; the four populations \
follow classical Bayes and the odd-parity coherence rides the geometric mean, \
which is the whole content of ",
 Cell[BoxData["twoQubitStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c7a415c-3e53-b7cb-441a-5906bbe71d11"],
 ", and the concurrence they report is the very ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["max",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    RowBox[{GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
         RowBox[{"01", ",", "10"}]]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "-", 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"00", ",", "00"}]], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"11", ",", "11"}]]}]]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "417aec05-2fbb-8238-7719-066f4a4fd102"],
 " we built in Section 16. The most-likely-path analysis of their ensemble \
splits into three branches, the high-concurrence odd branch hugging the \
ceiling and the two low-concurrence branches collapsing to the product states \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4705486f-1ac0-4964-6d3b-62499f75184e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3af5a034-7641-6879-6a8a-3a7e03f43b43"],
 ", matching the bimodal histogram. And Part II is the same physics seen the \
other way: there one qubit is watched along two incompatible axes and \
diffuses on a great circle; here two qubits are watched along one parity axis \
and are steered into a Bell state. In both, the state is moved not by any \
Hamiltonian but by the information a noisy record carries, folded back by \
Bayes' rule."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1641757231,ExpressionUUID->"68379bed-79e9-22be-19cc-12b77f9c7084"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Section",
 CellID->896279625,ExpressionUUID->"460eb9f9-c41e-8ef4-6e35-30a2eda8d4de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You now have a computation-first toolkit for continuous quantum measurement \
built from one Gaussian measurement operator and run in three settings. One \
qubit and one detector give the Bayes kick on the populations with the \
coherence riding along, the Rabi split, the ideality-capped purity, the \
Korotkov-Averin spectrum and its factor of four, and the phase back-action \
that completes the Kraus operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "258251be-7c16-7495-53b2-48f875a35eff"],
 ". Two detectors on non-commuting axes turn that operator on twice and watch \
collapse give way to great-circle diffusion, with an uncertainty floor that \
forbids the walk from stopping and output correlators whose zero-lag \
cross-value reads the angle between the axes. One detector on two qubits with \
a blind spot turns the same operator into a half-parity meter that steers the \
pair into a Bell state, with a closed-form concurrence ceiling recovered from \
the records. Each generalization is the same update applied twice or applied \
to a larger space, and each has been carried out in a superconducting-qubit \
laboratory. Before closing, the load-bearing results computed along the way:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1264190945,ExpressionUUID->"35c1f832-722b-ca69-63fe-f27c07df98b3"],

Cell["\<\
Information is the shrinking overlap of two Gaussians; with no Hamiltonian \
the populations follow Gaussian Bayes and localize to a pole with the \
Born-rule probability.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1806910998,ExpressionUUID->"7b6a50da-eb07-3910-296a-49878eb3887a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ideal detector conserves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "01"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23591dbb-79d4-ec10-5166-94e57866b77a"],
 ", so a pure state stays pure along a single record; the ensemble dephases \
only because runs localize differently."
}], "Item",
 CellID->962064851,ExpressionUUID->"114fd905-c79d-9420-4774-d16ef229ff0a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output spectrum's coherent line is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0047a90f-9cb0-808d-307c-4169154ad2d7"],
 " above the floor, at most four and at most two for a phase-preserving \
amplifier, half of it the nonclassical noise-backaction correlation; a naive \
Ito stepper that drops the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42e32fd7-26e6-6b71-7290-c6915293365b"],
 " drift loses the entire ensemble dephasing."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1660212291,ExpressionUUID->"4a2652ed-88d4-efb2-7bde-4bb72966b598"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every measurement is one Kraus operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0962d9db-7466-8598-3f11-d0857d10efe2"],
 ", the phase kick times the informational Bayes factor."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1553450743,ExpressionUUID->"5b3d557b-19e1-b503-0ac3-4d259f951c69"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two Kraus operators on non-commuting axes fail to commute by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["sinh",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "529c5c95-0588-d8f1-02a4-55dfac22aadb"],
 "; orthogonal detectors keep a pure state pure while forcing great-circle \
diffusion, bounded below by the commutator, with a steady Bloch length set by \
the balance between record-driven purification and the undelivered \
information."
}], "Item",
 CellID->376345483,ExpressionUUID->"18bedc4a-f6ca-97e0-4845-d617837cfdca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two output correlators are sums of exponentials with rates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "\[MinusPlus]", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f18273e-5cf5-00f5-0527-bf78548052df"],
 "; at zero lag the cross-correlator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CurlyPhi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1890d11b-851d-d227-48af-c9452ca9a10d"],
 ", and its antisymmetrized part reads a hidden slow rotation, the same \
cross-correlators that serve as a Bacon-Shor code's error syndromes."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1917523023,ExpressionUUID->"5b8be800-baff-aedd-0988-026a3e8bf427"],

Cell["\<\
A half-parity meter's odd-parity coherence rides the geometric mean of its \
two populations, the single-qubit ride-along one level up, so a measurement \
alone leaves a Bell state; the concurrence it reaches has a sharp closed-form \
ceiling and a bimodal final distribution.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->225924774,ExpressionUUID->"224fae0e-4768-b263-5274-406872020149"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The natural continuations are the pieces the essay still sets aside: a \
finite detector bandwidth, where the qubit and the cavity field must be \
tracked together; real-time feedback to lock the Rabi oscillation or \
stabilize the entanglement instead of only heralding it; and the many-qubit \
parity measurements that turn the single joint check of Part III into the \
continuously monitored error syndrome of a stabilizer code, where it meets \
the Bacon-Shor gauge qubit of Part II. This Bayesian-update view is also the \
sibling of the stochastic-differential-equation essays in this folder, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", " ", "vs", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Ito", "/"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d32ba1d-71ed-60b8-64c1-3c4707983282"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Manual", " ", "StepLike", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Ito", "/"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ccd4f42-4869-4b08-64f3-672c691c1652"],
 ", which integrate the same physics as a Bloch-Langevin equation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1508526016,ExpressionUUID->"0cf63df4-f608-7ba6-348d-b4b183bd498c"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"60948258-d69f-7f2c-10ab-2405e32a4276"
]
